emaining` — generic rate limiting used by core and extensions"},"670":{"id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference-90","page_id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference#operational","content":"Table"},"671":{"id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference-91","page_id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference#operational","content":"Columns"},"672":{"id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference-92","page_id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference#operational","content":"`wc_webhooks`"},"673":{"id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference-93","page_id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference#operational","content":"`webhook_id, status, name, user_id, delivery_url, secret, topic, date_created(_gmt), date_modified(_gmt), api_version, failure_count, pending_delivery`"},"674":{"id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference-94","page_id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference#operational","content":"`woocommerce_log`"},"675":{"id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference-95","page_id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference#operational","content":"`log_id, timestamp, level, source, message, context` — the WooCommerce → Status → Logs viewer reads this"},"676":{"id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference-96","page_id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference#operational","content":"Table shapes here come from `WC_Install::get_schema()` and the HPOS\ncolumn-mapping constants for this release. A few tables are created but\npopulated only once a related feature is active (`wc_product_attributes_lookup`,\n`wc_rate_limits`) — an empty table is not necessarily a bug."},"677":{"id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference-97","page_id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference#related","content":"<Card title=\"Database\" href=\"/docs/data-storage/database\" description=\"The concepts and judgment calls behind this schema.\" />"},"678":{"id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference-98","page_id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference#related","content":"<Card title=\"HPOS\" href=\"/docs/data-storage/hpos\" description=\"The order tables above, in depth — modes, migration, dual-mode code.\" />"},"679":{"id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference-99","page_id":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/data-storage/schema-reference#related","content":"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Data Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model\" description=\"The entities these tables back.\" />"},"680":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","type":"page","content":"AJAX","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/ajax"},"681":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-0","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax","content":"How WooCommerce does AJAX — the admin-ajax endpoint, WooCommerce's own wc-ajax fast path, nonces and the params objects, the built-in cart/checkout AJAX actions, and how to add your own safely."},"682":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-1","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/ajax#two-transports","content":"Two transports"},"683":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-2","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"Nonces and the params objects"},"684":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-3","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/ajax#adding-your-own-front-end-ajax","content":"Adding your own front-end AJAX"},"685":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-4","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/ajax#cart-fragments","content":"Cart fragments"},"686":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-5","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/ajax#blocks-note","content":"Blocks note"},"687":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-6","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/ajax#related","content":"Related"},"688":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-7","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax","content":"WooCommerce uses AJAX heavily on the classic front-end: adding to cart from a\nloop, updating quantities, applying coupons, refreshing the checkout totals.\nThere are **two** transports, and knowing which one an action uses tells you\nwhere to hook it."},"689":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-8","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#two-transports","content":"The public front-end actions routed through &#x2A;*`wc-ajax`** are:\n`get_refreshed_fragments`, `add_to_cart`, `remove_from_cart`,\n`apply_coupon`, `remove_coupon`, `update_shipping_method`, `get_cart_totals`,\n`update_order_review`, `checkout`, `get_variation`, and\n`get_customer_location`. `WC_AJAX` also registers each of these as\n`wp_ajax_woocommerce_<action>` and `wp_ajax_nopriv_woocommerce_<action>` so\nthey still work over `admin-ajax.php`."},"690":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-9","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"Front-end scripts receive their endpoint URLs and nonces from small localized\nobjects that WooCommerce prints:"},"691":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-10","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"Object"},"692":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-11","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"Attached to handle"},"693":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-12","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"Notable keys"},"694":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-13","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`woocommerce_params`"},"695":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-14","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`woocommerce`"},"696":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-15","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`ajax_url`, `wc_ajax_url`"},"697":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-16","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`wc_add_to_cart_params`"},"698":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-17","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`wc-add-to-cart`"},"699":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-18","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`ajax_url`, `wc_ajax_url`, `cart_url`, `is_cart`"},"700":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-19","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`wc_cart_params`"},"701":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-20","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`wc-cart`"},"702":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-21","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`ajax_url`, `wc_ajax_url`, `update_shipping_method_nonce`, `apply_coupon_nonce`, `remove_coupon_nonce`"},"703":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-22","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`wc_cart_fragments_params`"},"704":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-23","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`wc-cart-fragments`"},"705":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-24","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`ajax_url`, `wc_ajax_url`, `cart_hash_key`, `fragment_name`, `request_timeout`"},"706":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-25","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`wc_checkout_params`"},"707":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-26","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`wc-checkout`"},"708":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-27","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`ajax_url`, `wc_ajax_url`, `update_order_review_nonce`, `apply_coupon_nonce`, `remove_coupon_nonce`, `checkout_url`, `option_guest_checkout`"},"709":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-28","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`wc_country_select_params` / `wc_address_i18n_params`"},"710":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-29","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"`wc-country-select` / `wc-address-i18n`"},"711":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-30","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"country/state data, locale field ordering"},"712":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-31","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"WooCommerce passes each nonce in the request's `security` field and checks it\nserver-side with `check_ajax_referer( '<action>', 'security' )`. Under the\nCheckout Block none of these apply — the Store API uses its own\n`Nonce` / `Cart-Token` headers."},"713":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-32","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"For your own handlers, verify with `check_ajax_referer( 'your-action', 'security' )`\n(or `wp_verify_nonce()`), then a capability check where the action is not\npurely public."},"714":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-33","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#nonces-and-the-params-objects","content":"An AJAX handler with no nonce check and no capability check is a CSRF hole —\nworse if it writes data or reveals another customer's order. Every custom\nhandler: nonce first, capability second, then the work."},"715":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-34","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#adding-your-own-front-end-ajax","content":"Use the `wc-ajax` path instead when the call is high-frequency and does not\nneed the admin environment. It fires **one** hook for logged-in and guest\nusers alike:"},"716":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-35","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#adding-your-own-front-end-ajax","content":"There is no `wc_ajax_nopriv_*` hook. If you register only `wc_ajax_<action>`,\nguests reach it too — so your nonce and capability checks are the only gate."},"717":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-36","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#cart-fragments","content":"The mini-cart / cart-count updates after an AJAX add-to-cart come from the\n**cart fragments** system: `get_refreshed_fragments` returns an array of\n`selector => html`, filtered by `woocommerce_add_to_cart_fragments`, and the\n`wc-cart-fragments` script swaps each selector's contents and caches the\nresult in `sessionStorage`. Details and its performance cost are on the\nJavaScript page."},"718":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-37","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#blocks-note","content":"The Cart and Checkout &#x2A;*Blocks do not use `wc-ajax`.** They use the\nStore API (`/wp-json/wc/store/v1/…`)\nwith a cart token. A custom `wc_ajax_*` handler you wrote for the classic\ncheckout will not run under the Block."},"719":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-38","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#related","content":"<Card title=\"JavaScript\" href=\"/docs/development/javascript\" description=\"The client half — scripts, events, and cart fragments.\" />"},"720":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-39","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#related","content":"<Card title=\"REST API\" href=\"/docs/development/rest-api\" description=\"The Store API that replaces wc-ajax under the Blocks.\" />"},"721":{"id":"/docs/development/ajax-40","page_id":"/docs/development/ajax","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/ajax#related","content":"<Card title=\"Hooks (Actions)\" href=\"/docs/development/hooks\" description=\"Registering the wc_ajax_* / wp_ajax_* handlers your endpoints hang off.\" />"},"722":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","type":"page","content":"Blocks","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/blocks"},"723":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-0","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks","content":"The WooCommerce Cart and Checkout Blocks as an extension surface — block settings, Slot/Fill, checkout filters, inner blocks, the PHP IntegrationInterface, the Store API, and the client-side data stores."},"724":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-1","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/blocks#why-the-extension-model-is-different","content":"Why the extension model is different"},"725":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-2","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/blocks#the-extension-surface","content":"The extension surface"},"726":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-3","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/blocks#a-minimal-slotfill","content":"A minimal Slot/Fill"},"727":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-4","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"Reading cart / checkout state"},"728":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-5","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/blocks#server-side-attach-and-receive-data","content":"Server side: attach and receive data"},"729":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-6","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/blocks#decision-guide","content":"Decision guide"},"730":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-7","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/blocks#related","content":"Related"},"731":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-8","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks","content":"The **Cart and Checkout Blocks** are the React storefront that replaced the\nclassic shortcode pages on new installs from WooCommerce 8.3. They render in\nthe browser and talk to the Store API.\nThey are **not** extended with PHP template hooks — a different set of APIs\ndoes the equivalent jobs."},"732":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-9","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#why-the-extension-model-is-different","content":"Classic hooks like `woocommerce_checkout_fields`,\n`woocommerce_review_order_before_payment`, and\n`woocommerce_checkout_order_processed` **do not fire** under the Block. Their\nreplacements are below and on the Hooks page."},"733":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-10","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#a-minimal-slotfill","content":"The four fills are `ExperimentalOrderMeta` (below the order summary, above\nProceed to Checkout), `ExperimentalOrderShippingPackages` (the shipping step),\n`ExperimentalOrderLocalPickupPackages` (the pickup-options block), and\n`ExperimentalDiscountsMeta` (below the coupon-code input). Import from\n`@woocommerce/blocks-checkout` (webpack-aliased to `window.wc.blocksCheckout`);\nrender via `registerPlugin` with `scope: 'woocommerce-checkout'`."},"734":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-11","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"Client code reads state from `@wordpress/data` stores, not from globals:"},"735":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-12","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"Store"},"736":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-13","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"Holds"},"737":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-14","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"`wc/store/cart`"},"738":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-15","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"Cart items, totals, coupons, shipping rates, customer address"},"739":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-16","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"`wc/store/checkout`"},"740":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-17","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"Checkout status, order ID, custom extension data"},"741":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-18","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"`wc/store/payment`"},"742":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-19","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"Selected payment method, payment status"},"743":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-20","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"`wc/store/validation`"},"744":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-21","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"Field validation errors"},"745":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-22","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#reading-cart--checkout-state","content":"Read them with `select()` / `useSelect()` from `@wordpress/data`. WooCommerce's\ndocs now steer extensions to the data stores rather than internal hooks like\n`useStoreCart` from `@woocommerce/base-context`. `@woocommerce/settings`\n(`wc.wcSettings`) exposes `getSetting()` for values your `IntegrationInterface`\npassed from PHP."},"746":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-23","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#server-side-attach-and-receive-data","content":"`endpoint` takes a schema identifier — use the `::IDENTIFIER` constant on the\nroute schema class (`CartSchema`, `CheckoutSchema`, `ProductSchema`, …) rather\nthan a literal string. `woocommerce_store_api_register_update_callback()` is\ninvoked through the `POST wc/store/v1/cart/extensions` endpoint (and\n`batch`)."},"747":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-24","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#server-side-attach-and-receive-data","content":"Declare compatibility so the merchant can use the Blocks with your plugin\nactive — see\nArchitecture → bootstrap\n(`cart_checkout_blocks` feature slug)."},"748":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-25","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#decision-guide","content":"The Blocks APIs move faster than core PHP and the Slot/Fill names are still\nexported as `Experimental*`. The names here match the WooCommerce Blocks\ndocumentation; treat them as unstable, build against a pinned WooCommerce\nversion, and re-test on each minor upgrade."},"749":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-26","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#related","content":"<Card title=\"REST API\" href=\"/docs/development/rest-api\" description=\"The Store API that the Blocks read from and post to.\" />"},"750":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-27","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#related","content":"<Card title=\"JavaScript\" href=\"/docs/development/javascript\" description=\"The classic front-end JS the Blocks replace, and where each still applies.\" />"},"751":{"id":"/docs/development/blocks-28","page_id":"/docs/development/blocks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/blocks#related","content":"<Card title=\"Hooks (Actions)\" href=\"/docs/development/hooks\" description=\"Which classic hooks stop firing once the Block is active.\" />"},"752":{"id":"/docs/development/filters","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","type":"page","content":"Filters","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/filters"},"753":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-0","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters","content":"How WooCommerce filters work — transforming a value on its way through core, the return-value contract, priority and arguments, the WC_Data dynamic getter filters, and the mistakes that make a filter silently wrong."},"754":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-1","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/filters#the-contract","content":"The contract"},"755":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-2","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/filters#the-wc_data-dynamic-getter-filters","content":"The `WC_Data` dynamic getter filters"},"756":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-3","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/filters#value-vs-display--the-recurring-trap","content":"Value vs. display — the recurring trap"},"757":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-4","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/filters#removing-a-filter","content":"Removing a filter"},"758":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-5","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/filters#finding-filters","content":"Finding filters"},"759":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-6","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/filters#related","content":"Related"},"760":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-7","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters","content":"A **filter** is a value passing through a named checkpoint:\n`$value = apply_filters( 'filter_name', $value, ...$context )`. Your callback\nreceives the value, returns a possibly-changed version, and WooCommerce uses\nwhat you return. Filters are how you change *what something is* — a price, a\nlabel, a list of fields, a query — without editing core."},"761":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-8","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters","content":"For making something *happen*, use an action."},"762":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-9","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#the-contract","content":"A filter callback that does not return sets the value to\nnull. This is the most common filter bug: an early\nreturn;, a missing return on one branch, or a\nvar\\_dump() left in. The button vanishes, the price becomes\nempty, the field list is wiped."},"763":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-10","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#the-contract","content":"**Priority** and **accepted args** work exactly as for actions — argument 3\nand 4 of `add_filter()`. Ask for every context parameter you need; they are\nonly passed up to the count you declare."},"764":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-11","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#the-contract","content":"**Type matters.** If the value is an array, return an array. If it is a\nformatted HTML string, return a string. Returning the wrong type pushes a\nbug downstream to wherever the value is finally used."},"765":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-12","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#the-wc_data-dynamic-getter-filters","content":"Product, order, and coupon objects run **every getter through a filter** named\n`woocommerce_<object_type>_get_<property>` — for example\n`woocommerce_product_get_price`, `woocommerce_order_get_total`,\n`woocommerce_coupon_get_amount`. This is why you filter a product's price with\n`woocommerce_product_get_price` rather than hunting for where the catalog\nrenders it."},"766":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-13","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#the-wc_data-dynamic-getter-filters","content":"These getter filters fire constantly — in loops, in the\nadmin, during totals calculation, in REST responses. Keep the callback\ncheap, guard against empty values, and never call the same getter inside the\nfilter (infinite recursion). For cart-line pricing, prefer setting the price\nonce on woocommerce\\_before\\_calculate\\_totals — see\nDeveloper Mental Model."},"767":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-14","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#removing-a-filter","content":"Same rule as `remove_action()`: exact callback identifier, exact priority. If\na plugin adds the filter on a hook like `init`, you must remove it on a\n*later* hook so your `remove_filter()` runs after their `add_filter()`."},"768":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-15","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#finding-filters","content":"Search the WooCommerce source for `apply_filters(` near the value you care\nabout. Every filter's name and its context parameters are right there."},"769":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-16","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#finding-filters","content":"The pattern is `woocommerce_<object_type>_get_<prop>`, applied by\n`WC_Data::get_prop()` for every simple stored property — so you can usually\nderive the name from the getter (`get_stock_status()` →\n`woocommerce_product_get_stock_status`). The **computed** getters are the\nexception — they carry their own hand-written filter names, e.g.\n`get_price_html()` → `woocommerce_get_price_html`. When in doubt, grep the\nclass for `apply_filters`."},"770":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-17","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#finding-filters","content":"Query Monitor shows filters as well as actions for the current request."},"771":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-18","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#related","content":"<Card title=\"Hooks (Actions)\" href=\"/docs/development/hooks\" description=\"The other half of the system — behavior instead of value transformation.\" />"},"772":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-19","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#related","content":"<Card title=\"Developer Mental Model\" href=\"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model\" description=\"Why the value layer and the display layer must not be confused.\" />"},"773":{"id":"/docs/development/filters-20","page_id":"/docs/development/filters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/filters#related","content":"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Data Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model\" description=\"The WC_Data objects whose getters these filters wrap.\" />"},"774":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","type":"page","content":"Hooks (Actions)","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/hooks"},"775":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-0","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks","content":"How WooCommerce action hooks work — registering and removing callbacks, priority and argument count, finding the right hook, and debugging which hooks actually fire on a given request."},"776":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-1","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/hooks#the-mechanics","content":"The mechanics"},"777":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-2","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/hooks#removing-and-replacing-core-callbacks","content":"Removing and replacing core callbacks"},"778":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-3","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/hooks#finding-the-right-hook","content":"Finding the right hook"},"779":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-4","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"Debugging which hooks fire"},"780":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-5","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/hooks#related","content":"Related"},"781":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-6","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks","content":"An **action** is a named moment in execution where WooCommerce (or WordPress)\ncalls `do_action( 'hook_name', ...$args )`. Any code registered against that\nname runs at that point. Actions are how you make something *happen* —\noutput markup, send a message, write a record — without editing core."},"782":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-7","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks","content":"For changing a *value*, you want a filter, not an\naction."},"783":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-8","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#the-mechanics","content":"**Argument 3 — priority** (default `10`). Lower runs earlier. Core often\nhooks its own output at `10`; use `9` to go before it, `11` to go after."},"784":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-9","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#the-mechanics","content":"**Argument 4 — accepted args** (default `1`). WooCommerce may pass several\nparameters to an action; you only receive the number you declare. Declaring\ntoo few is a silent bug — the later parameters are simply not passed."},"785":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-10","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#the-mechanics","content":"The callback's &#x2A;*return value is ignored.** Returning something from an\naction callback does nothing."},"786":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-11","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#the-mechanics","content":"Register hooks from a plugin or mu-plugin, not a theme, unless\nthe behavior is purely presentational and tied to that theme. Commerce logic\nin functions.php disappears when the theme is switched."},"787":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-12","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#removing-and-replacing-core-callbacks","content":"To change what a core action *does*, remove its callback and add your own. You\nmust match the **exact** callback identifier and priority used in core."},"788":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-13","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#removing-and-replacing-core-callbacks","content":"remove\\_action() for a **method on an object instance**\n(e.g. \\[ WC()->something, 'method' ]) needs a reference to the\nsame instance and the same priority. If core refactors how it registers that\ncallback, your remove\\_action() silently stops matching and the\noriginal behavior returns. Re-check on WooCommerce updates."},"789":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-14","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#finding-the-right-hook","content":"Practical tools:"},"790":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-15","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#finding-the-right-hook","content":"**WooCommerce templates** carry `do_action()` calls with clear names\n(`woocommerce_before_main_content`, `woocommerce_single_product_summary`, …).\nThe template file *is* the hook map for classic output."},"791":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-16","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#finding-the-right-hook","content":"**`plugins/woocommerce/includes/wc-template-hooks.php`** wires core\ncallbacks to those actions — read it to see what already runs at each\nposition and at what priority (the callback bodies are in\n`wc-template-functions.php`)."},"792":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-17","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#finding-the-right-hook","content":"**Query Monitor** (plugin) lists every hook fired on the current request,\nwith callbacks and file references."},"793":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-18","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#finding-the-right-hook","content":"**`all` hook** — for a one-off trace, `add_action( 'all', … )` logs every\nhook name. Noisy; never ship it."},"794":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-19","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"Common reasons a hook \"doesn't fire\":"},"795":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-20","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"Symptom"},"796":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-21","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"Cause"},"797":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-22","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"Nothing happens at all"},"798":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-23","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"Callback registered *after* the action already ran — register earlier (e.g. on `init`)"},"799":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-24","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"Works on the front end, not in admin/REST/cron"},"800":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-25","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"That action only fires in a front-end request context"},"801":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-26","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"Worked before Blocks"},"802":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-27","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"It is a classic cart/checkout hook; the Block does not fire it (see Blocks)"},"803":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-28","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"Fires but output is missing"},"804":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-29","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"Wrong priority — another callback removed or overwrote it later"},"805":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-30","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#debugging-which-hooks-fire","content":"WooCommerce instantiates `WC_Deprecated_Action_Hooks` and\n`WC_Deprecated_Filter_Hooks` (both extend `WC_Deprecated_Hooks`) during\n`WooCommerce::init()`. They map a set of renamed hooks to their replacements\nand emit a `_deprecated_hook()` notice when the old name is used. Do not rely\non this shim — treat a deprecation notice as \"fix this now\"."},"806":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-31","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#related","content":"<Card title=\"Filters\" href=\"/docs/development/filters\" description=\"The other half of the hook system — changing a value instead of adding behavior.\" />"},"807":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-32","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#related","content":"<Card title=\"Templates\" href=\"/docs/development/templates\" description=\"Where most classic action hooks are fired from.\" />"},"808":{"id":"/docs/development/hooks-33","page_id":"/docs/development/hooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/hooks#related","content":"<Card title=\"Where Does This Come From?\" href=\"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from\" description=\"The locate-before-you-edit pattern hook discovery is part of.\" />"},"809":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","type":"page","content":"JavaScript","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/javascript"},"810":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript-0","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/javascript","content":"WooCommerce's front-end JavaScript — the core script handles, the jQuery events fired on document.body for cart and checkout, the cart fragments system and its cost, and how the Blocks change the picture."},"811":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript-1","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/javascript#core-script-handles","content":"Core script handles"},"812":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript-2","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/javascript#the-event-bus","content":"The event bus"},"813":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript-3","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/javascript#cart-fragments","content":"Cart fragments"},"814":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript-4","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/javascript#blocks-reading-state-in-js","content":"Blocks: reading state in JS"},"815":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript-5","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/javascript#related","content":"Related"},"816":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript-6","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/javascript","content":"The classic WooCommerce front-end ships a set of jQuery-based scripts that\ndrive add-to-cart, the cart page, the checkout, variation selection, and the\ncountry/state selects. They communicate through &#x2A;*events fired on\n`document.body`** — that event bus is the main integration point."},"817":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript-7","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/javascript","content":"The Cart and Checkout Blocks replace most of this\nwith React and `@wordpress/data`; the split is noted throughout."},"818":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript-8","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/javascript#core-script-handles","content":"Enqueue your script with the relevant handle as a dependency so it loads\nafter WooCommerce's:"},"819":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript-9","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/javascript#core-script-handles","content":"Handle"},"820":{"id":"/docs/development/javascript-10","page_id":"/docs/development/javascript","tags":