st-api-28","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#wcv3-rest-api","content":"Store config, the status report as JSON, reference data"},"922":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-29","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#wcv3-rest-api","content":"The **Analytics** reports live under a separate namespace,\n`/wp-json/wc-analytics/…` (`reports/orders`, `reports/products`,\n`reports/revenue`, …), plus `imports/status` and `imports/retry-failed` added\nin WooCommerce 11.0 for managing failed historical-data imports."},"923":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-30","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#auth","content":"**API keys** — generated at WooCommerce → Settings → Advanced → REST API, as\na consumer key / consumer secret pair with a Read / Write / Read-Write\nscope. Sent over HTTPS as HTTP Basic auth or as query parameters on\nnon-HTTPS (discouraged)."},"924":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-31","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#auth","content":"**Cookie auth + nonce** — for same-origin requests from a logged-in admin\n(e.g. a custom admin screen), send the `X-WP-Nonce` header from\n`wp_create_nonce( 'wp_rest' )`."},"925":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-32","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#auth","content":"API keys are full credentials for whatever scope they carry. A Read-Write\nkey can create orders and read every customer's PII. Scope them minimally,\nstore them as secrets, and revoke unused ones."},"926":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-33","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#store-api","content":"Base: `/wp-json/wc/store/v1/`. Main endpoints: `cart`, `cart/add-item`,\n`cart/update-item`, `cart/remove-item`, `cart/apply-coupon`,\n`cart/remove-coupon`, `cart/update-customer`, `cart/select-shipping-rate`,\n`cart/extensions`, `checkout`, `batch`, `products`, `products/attributes`,\n`products/categories`, `products/collection-data`, `products/reviews`."},"927":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-34","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#store-api","content":"It is **stateful*&#x2A;: a &#x2A;*`Cart-Token`** header (a JWT, returned on the first\n`GET /cart` response) identifies the\nWooCommerce session, so\n`POST wc/store/v1/cart/add-item` mutates *this visitor's* cart. `POST` to\n`/cart/*` and all `/checkout&#x60; requests also require a &#x2A;*`Nonce`** header —\nunless a `Cart-Token` is supplied, in which case the nonce is not needed.\nThis is why the Store API is safe to call from the browser and is not a\ngeneral integration API."},"928":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-35","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#store-api","content":"Extend it with `ExtendSchema` rather than raw filters — see\nBlocks → server side."},"929":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-36","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#adding-a-custom-route","content":"Neither API is designed for you to bolt resources onto. For custom endpoints,\nregister your own namespace with WordPress core's `register_rest_route()`:"},"930":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-37","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#adding-a-custom-route","content":"A route with 'permission\\_callback' => '\\_\\_return\\_true' is\npublic. If it reads or writes store data, that is a data-exposure bug.\nAlways supply a real permission callback."},"931":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-38","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#adding-a-custom-route","content":"You can reuse WooCommerce's CRUD objects (`wc_get_product()`,\n`wc_get_order()`) inside your callback — do not query tables directly."},"932":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-39","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#related","content":"<Card title=\"Blocks\" href=\"/docs/development/blocks\" description=\"The Store API's primary consumer, and how to extend its schema.\" />"},"933":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-40","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#related","content":"<Card title=\"AJAX\" href=\"/docs/development/ajax\" description=\"The classic-front-end transport the Store API replaces under Blocks.\" />"},"934":{"id":"/docs/development/rest-api-41","page_id":"/docs/development/rest-api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/rest-api#related","content":"<Card title=\"WordPress Fundamentals\" href=\"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals\" description=\"The WordPress REST layer both APIs are built on.\" />"},"935":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","type":"page","content":"Shortcodes","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/shortcodes"},"936":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-0","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes","content":"The WooCommerce shortcodes — the page shortcodes that back the classic cart, checkout, and account pages, the product-display shortcodes, how they are registered, and how the Blocks migration changes their role."},"937":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-1","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"Page shortcodes"},"938":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-2","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"Product-display shortcodes"},"939":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-3","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#registering-your-own","content":"Registering your own"},"940":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-4","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#related","content":"Related"},"941":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-5","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes","content":"A shortcode is a `[bracketed]` token in post content that WordPress replaces\nwith rendered output. WooCommerce registers a set of them through the\n`WC_Shortcodes` class on `init`. Two groups matter for different reasons."},"942":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-6","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"The classic Cart, Checkout, and My Account pages are **just WordPress pages\ncontaining one shortcode**:"},"943":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-7","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"Shortcode"},"944":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-8","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"Renders"},"945":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-9","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"Backing method"},"946":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-10","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"`[woocommerce_cart]`"},"947":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-11","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"The cart page"},"948":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-12","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"`WC_Shortcodes::cart()`"},"949":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-13","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"`[woocommerce_checkout]`"},"950":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-14","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"The checkout page"},"951":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-15","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"`WC_Shortcodes::checkout()`"},"952":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-16","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"`[woocommerce_my_account]`"},"953":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-17","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"The account dashboard, orders, addresses"},"954":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-18","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"`WC_Shortcodes::my_account()`"},"955":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-19","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"`[woocommerce_order_tracking]`"},"956":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-20","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"The order-status lookup form"},"957":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-21","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"`WC_Shortcodes::order_tracking()`"},"958":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-22","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"WooCommerce stores which page holds which shortcode in options\n(`woocommerce_cart_page_id`, `woocommerce_checkout_page_id`,\n`woocommerce_myaccount_page_id`). Those page IDs — not the shortcode text —\nare how core builds cart/checkout URLs and redirects."},"959":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-23","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#page-shortcodes","content":"Removing the shortcode from the page, or deleting the page, breaks checkout\nrouting even if another page renders a cart. Repair from **WooCommerce →\nStatus → Tools*&#x2A;, the &#x2A;*\"Create default WooCommerce pages\"** tool (its button\nreads *Create pages*) — it recreates only missing pages and does not\noverwrite existing ones."},"960":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-24","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"For putting products into arbitrary content (a landing page, a blog post):"},"961":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-25","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"Shortcode"},"962":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-26","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"Output"},"963":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-27","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"`[products]`"},"964":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-28","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"A configurable product grid — the modern, unified one (attributes: `ids`, `category`, `tag`, `limit`, `columns`, `orderby`, `on_sale`, `best_selling`, `top_rated`, …)"},"965":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-29","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"`[product_page id=\"99\"]`"},"966":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-30","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"A full single-product layout for one product"},"967":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-31","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"`[add_to_cart id=\"99\"]`"},"968":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-32","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"Price + add-to-cart button for one product"},"969":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-33","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"`[add_to_cart_url id=\"99\"]`"},"970":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-34","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"Just the add-to-cart URL"},"971":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-35","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"`[product_categories]` / `[product_category]`"},"972":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-36","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"Category tiles / a single category's products"},"973":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-37","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"`[product]`, `[featured_products]`, `[sale_products]`, `[best_selling_products]`, `[top_rated_products]`, `[recent_products]`, `[related_products]`, `[product_attribute]`"},"974":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-38","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"Still registered in 11.0.1 — all handled internally by the same `[products]` renderer with preset attributes"},"975":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-39","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"`[shop_messages]`"},"976":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-40","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"WooCommerce notices (for full-site-editing themes)"},"977":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-41","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"The full set is registered in `WC_Shortcodes::init()`. The `[products]` query\ncan be filtered:"},"978":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-42","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#product-display-shortcodes","content":"`apply_filters( 'woocommerce_shortcode_products_query', $query_args, $atts, $type )`\nis called from `WC_Shortcode_Products::parse_query_args()`."},"979":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-43","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#registering-your-own","content":"Nothing WooCommerce-specific — use WordPress's `add_shortcode()`. If your\noutput depends on the cart or customer, make sure the shortcode is not\nrunning in a context where `WC()->cart` is null, and remember shortcode output\nis often **cached** with the page."},"980":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-44","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#registering-your-own","content":"Shortcodes that render per-visitor data (cart contents, \"hello, name\") fight\nfull-page caching. Either exclude the page from cache or move the dynamic\npart to a cart fragment / Store API call."},"981":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-45","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#related","content":"<Card title=\"Blocks\" href=\"/docs/development/blocks\" description=\"What replaced the cart/checkout shortcodes on modern installs.\" />"},"982":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-46","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#related","content":"<Card title=\"Templates\" href=\"/docs/development/templates\" description=\"How the page shortcodes render their output.\" />"},"983":{"id":"/docs/development/shortcodes-47","page_id":"/docs/development/shortcodes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/shortcodes#related","content":"<Card title=\"JavaScript\" href=\"/docs/development/javascript\" description=\"Cart fragments — the caching-safe way to show per-visitor data.\" />"},"984":{"id":"/docs/development/templates","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","type":"page","content":"Templates","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/templates"},"985":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-0","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates","content":"The classic WooCommerce template system — how templates are located and loaded, the theme override mechanism, template parts, the variables in scope inside a template, the hooks fired from within them, and when not to override."},"986":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-1","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/templates#how-a-template-is-located","content":"How a template is located"},"987":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-2","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/templates#overriding-a-template-in-a-theme","content":"Overriding a template in a theme"},"988":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-3","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/templates#a-plugin-can-provide-templates-too","content":"A plugin can provide templates too"},"989":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-4","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"Variables in scope"},"990":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-5","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/templates#template-parts-and-hooks-inside-templates","content":"Template parts and hooks inside templates"},"991":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-6","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/templates#when-not-to-override","content":"When not to override"},"992":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-7","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/templates#related","content":"Related"},"993":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-8","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates","content":"WooCommerce's **classic** storefront is rendered from PHP template files. A\ntheme can replace any of them by providing its own copy. This is powerful and\nfrequently the *wrong* first choice — a hook or filter usually reaches what\nyou need without the maintenance cost."},"994":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-9","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates","content":"Templates apply to the classic front-end only. The\nCart and Checkout Blocks do not use them."},"995":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-10","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#how-a-template-is-located","content":"Core renders a fragment by calling `wc_get_template()` or\n`wc_get_template_part()`, which delegate path resolution to\n`wc_locate_template()`:"},"996":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-11","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#overriding-a-template-in-a-theme","content":"Find the source file under `plugins/woocommerce/templates/` — e.g.\n`templates/single-product/title.php`."},"997":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-12","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#overriding-a-template-in-a-theme","content":"Copy it to your theme, **dropping the `templates/` segment** and adding a\n`woocommerce/` prefix: `your-child-theme/woocommerce/single-product/title.php`."},"998":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-13","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#overriding-a-template-in-a-theme","content":"Edit your copy."},"999":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-14","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#overriding-a-template-in-a-theme","content":"You now maintain a fork of that file. Each core template has an\n@version docblock; WooCommerce → Status → System\nStatus lists every override whose version is behind core\n(\"version X is out of date. The core version is Y\"). When it flags\none, diff your copy against the new core file and re-apply your change. A\nstale override silently drops new markup, hooks, and accessibility fixes."},"1000":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-15","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#overriding-a-template-in-a-theme","content":"Before copying a template, check whether an action hook inside it, or a\nfilter on the value it prints, does the job. Overriding\nprice.php to change a price is almost always wrong — filter\nwoocommerce\\_get\\_price\\_html instead."},"1001":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-16","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#a-plugin-can-provide-templates-too","content":"The signature is\n`wc_get_template( $template_name, $args = array(), $template_path = '', $default_path = '' )`.\nA plugin that calls\n`wc_get_template( 'foo.php', $args, '', plugin_dir_path( __FILE__ ) . 'templates/' )`\nships its own default while `wc_locate_template()` still checks the theme's\n`woocommerce/foo.php` first — so themes can override plugin-provided templates\nexactly as they override core ones."},"1002":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-17","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"`wc_get_template( $name, $args )` runs `extract( $args )` before including the\nfile, so each key of `$args` becomes a local variable. Which keys exist is\n**per template** — read the `wc_get_template()` call in core that renders it."},"1003":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-18","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"Common examples:"},"1004":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-19","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"Template"},"1005":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-20","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"In scope"},"1006":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-21","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"`single-product/*.php`"},"1007":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-22","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"`$product` (the global `$product` is also set)"},"1008":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-23","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"`cart/cart.php`"},"1009":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-24","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"no `$args`; reads `WC()->cart` directly"},"1010":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-25","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"`checkout/form-checkout.php`"},"1011":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-26","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"`$checkout` (a `WC_Checkout` instance)"},"1012":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-27","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"`emails/email-order-details.php`"},"1013":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-28","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"`$order`, `$sent_to_admin`, `$plain_text`, `$email`"},"1014":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-29","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"`cart/cart-totals.php`, `checkout/review-order.php`"},"1015":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-30","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"no `$args`; read `WC()->cart`"},"1016":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-31","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#variables-in-scope","content":"Each core template's docblock lists what it can rely on; the `wc_get_template()`\ncall site is the authoritative source."},"1017":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-32","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#template-parts-and-hooks-inside-templates","content":"**`wc_get_template_part( $slug, $name )`** loads content templates like\n`content-product.php` from the loop. Themes override these the same way."},"1018":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-33","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#template-parts-and-hooks-inside-templates","content":"Templates contain **`do_action()` calls** — these are the injection points\nyou should prefer over editing the file. `content-single-product.php` is\nalmost entirely `do_action( 'woocommerce_single_product_summary' )` and\nsiblings; the markup lives in hooked callbacks, not the template."},"1019":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-34","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#template-parts-and-hooks-inside-templates","content":"If you keep a template override, **keep its `do_action()` calls**. Removing\nthem silently disables every plugin (and core feature) that injects there."},"1020":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-35","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#related","content":"<Card title=\"Hooks (Actions)\" href=\"/docs/development/hooks\" description=\"The do_action() calls inside templates — the preferred alternative to overriding.\" />"},"1021":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-36","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#related","content":"<Card title=\"Blocks\" href=\"/docs/development/blocks\" description=\"The Cart/Checkout front-end that templates do not touch.\" />"},"1022":{"id":"/docs/development/templates-37","page_id":"/docs/development/templates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/templates#related","content":"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Extension Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/extension-model\" description=\"Where template overrides sit among the four mechanisms.\" />"},"1023":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","type":"page","content":"WooCommerce Extension Model","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model"},"1024":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-0","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","content":"The four ways WooCommerce lets you change its behavior — hooks, filters, template overrides, and blocks — what each one can and cannot do, how they compose, and how to choose between them."},"1025":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-1","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#the-four-mechanisms","content":"The four mechanisms"},"1026":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-2","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"Actions — change *what happens*"},"1027":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-3","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"Filters — change *a value*"},"1028":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-4","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions-vs-filters--the-test","content":"Actions vs filters — the test"},"1029":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-5","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#template-overrides--change-classic-markup","content":"Template overrides — change *classic markup*"},"1030":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-6","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#blocks--change-the-react-storefront","content":"Blocks — change *the React storefront*"},"1031":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-7","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#how-they-compose","content":"How they compose"},"1032":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-8","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#choosing-a-mechanism","content":"Choosing a mechanism"},"1033":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-9","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#where-each-mechanisms-code-belongs","content":"Where each mechanism's code belongs"},"1034":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-10","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#related","content":"Related"},"1035":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-11","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","content":"WooCommerce is built to be changed without editing it. There are four\nmechanisms for that, and they are not alternatives to pick from at random —\neach operates at a different layer, and real customizations often use two or\nthree together. This page is the map of the system; the Development section\n&#x2A;(planned)* documents each mechanism in depth."},"1036":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-12","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"An action is a point in execution where WooCommerce calls\n`do_action( 'some_hook', $context… )`. Your callback runs there for effect;\nits return value is discarded."},"1037":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-13","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"**Good for:** outputting extra markup at a known position, sending a\nnotification, writing a log row, creating related data when an order\ncompletes, enqueueing a script on WooCommerce pages."},"1038":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-14","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"**Cannot:** change a value WooCommerce already calculated. If the price is\nwrong, an action fired after pricing cannot fix it."},"1039":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-15","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"Representative core actions (all still present in 11.0.1):"},"1040":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-16","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"Action"},"1041":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-17","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"Position"},"1042":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-18","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"`woocommerce_before_add_to_cart_form` / `woocommerce_after_add_to_cart_button`"},"1043":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-19","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"Around the single-product add-to-cart form"},"1044":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-20","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"`woocommerce_single_product_summary`"},"1045":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-21","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"The product summary column (priced callbacks at set priorities: title 5, price 10, add-to-cart 30)"},"1046":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-22","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"`woocommerce_checkout_before_customer_details` / `woocommerce_review_order_before_payment`"},"1047":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-23","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"Classic checkout regions"},"1048":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-24","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"`woocommerce_checkout_create_order`"},"1049":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-25","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"Just before a new order is saved — set order data here"},"1050":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-26","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"`woocommerce_thankyou`"},"1051":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-27","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"The order-received page, with the order ID"},"1052":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-28","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"`woocommerce_order_status_changed`"},"1053":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-29","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions--change-what-happens","content":"Any order status transition"},"1054":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-30","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"A filter is `apply_filters( 'some_filter', $value, $context… )`. Your callback\nreceives `$value`, returns a (possibly modified) version, and WooCommerce uses\nwhat you return."},"1055":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-31","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"**Good for:** adjusting a price, relabelling a button, adding/removing\ncheckout fields, altering a product query, changing an email recipient,\ntoggling whether a gateway is available."},"1056":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-32","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"**Must:** always return a value — returning nothing sets it to `null` and\nbreaks everything downstream."},"1057":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-33","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"For a value change, a filter is almost always the correct mechanism and the\nhighest-safety one. It survives updates and touches nothing else."},"1058":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-34","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"Representative core filters (all still present in 11.0.1):"},"1059":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-35","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"Filter"},"1060":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-36","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"Changes"},"1061":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-37","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"`woocommerce_product_get_price` / `woocommerce_product_get_regular_price` / `woocommerce_product_get_sale_price`"},"1062":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-38","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"The stored price a `WC_Product` returns"},"1063":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-39","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"`woocommerce_get_price_html`"},"1064":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-40","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"The formatted price HTML shown in the catalog"},"1065":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-41","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"`woocommerce_cart_item_price` / `woocommerce_cart_item_subtotal`"},"1066":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-42","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"The *displayed* per-line price in the cart (not the amount charged — that is set via `set_price()` on `woocommerce_before_calculate_totals`)"},"1067":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-43","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"`woocommerce_checkout_fields`"},"1068":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-44","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"The classic checkout field definitions"},"1069":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-45","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"`woocommerce_available_payment_gateways`"},"1070":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-46","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"Which gateways are offered at checkout"},"1071":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-47","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"`woocommerce_email_recipient_<id>`"},"1072":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-48","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#filters--change-a-value","content":"The recipient of a given transactional email"},"1073":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-49","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions-vs-filters--the-test","content":"Action. Hook the position, echo or do your thing."},"1074":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-50","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions-vs-filters--the-test","content":"Filter. Hook the value, return the new one."},"1075":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-51","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#actions-vs-filters--the-test","content":"Stop — you are patching a symptom. Find the filter on the value."},"1076":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-52","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#template-overrides--change-classic-markup","content":"WooCommerce renders classic storefront fragments from PHP files in its\n`plugins/woocommerce/templates/` directory. Core loads them with\n`wc_get_template()` / `wc_get_template_part()`, which call `wc_locate_template()`\nto resolve the path — checking `yourtheme/woocommerce/<same-path>` first, then\nfalling back to the plugin. Copy a template into that theme folder (minus the\n`templates/` segment) and your copy wins. The resolution can also be filtered\nvia `woocommerce_locate_template` or `wc_get_template`."},"1077":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-53","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#template-overrides--change-classic-markup","content":"A template override is a **maintained fork of one file**. Each core template\ncarries an @version docblock; WooCommerce → Status → System\nStatus lists every overridden template whose @version is behind\nthe current core template (\"version X is out of date. The core version is\nY\"). When WooCommerce changes that template, your copy does not get the\nchange and can silently drop new markup, hooks, or accessibility fixes. Use\nonly when no hook or filter reaches what you need."},"1078":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-54","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#template-overrides--change-classic-markup","content":"Template overrides only affect the **classic** front-end. They do nothing to\nthe Cart and Checkout **Blocks** — a template override of `checkout/*.php`\nhas no effect on a store using the Checkout Block."},"1079":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-55","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#blocks--change-the-react-storefront","content":"The Cart and Checkout Blocks render on the client and get their data from the\nStore API. They are\nnot extended with PHP template hooks. Instead:"},"1080":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-56","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#how-they-compose","content":"Real customizations layer the mechanisms. A worked shape — adding a gift-wrap\noption to checkout:"},"1081":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-57","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#choosing-a-mechanism","content":"Use it. Done. Highest safety, zero maintenance."},"1082":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-58","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#choosing-a-mechanism","content":"Use the action at that position."},"1083":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-59","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#choosing-a-mechanism","content":"Override the template. Record it; re-check on every WooCommerce update."},"1084":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-60","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#choosing-a-mechanism","content":"Use block settings, then Slot/Fill, then the integration interface. Do not\nreach for PHP template overrides."},"1085":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-61","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#choosing-a-mechanism","content":"Stop. Re-scope the requirement, request an upstream hook, or build a proper\nextension around the constraint."},"1086":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-62","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#where-each-mechanisms-code-belongs","content":"The hook names, template functions, and Blocks APIs on this page were checked\nagainst WooCommerce 11.0.1. The Blocks `Experimental*` Slot/Fill names are\nstill marked experimental by WooCommerce and may be renamed in a future\nrelease — pin the WooCommerce Blocks version you build against."},"1087":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-63","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#related","content":"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Architecture\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture\" description=\"The shared core that all four mechanisms hook into.\" />"},"1088":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-64","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#related","content":"<Card title=\"Where Does This Come From?\" href=\"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from\" description=\"The pattern for finding which mechanism owns the thing you want to change.\" />"},"1089":{"id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model-65","page_id":"/docs/foundations/extension-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/extension-model#related","content":"<Card title=\"Documentation Design System\" href=\"/docs/about/design-system\" description=\"The SafetyLevel framework these choices are labelled with.\" />"},"1090":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","type":"page","content":"WooCommerce Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture"},"1091":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-0","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","content":"How WooCommerce boots inside a WordPress request, the WC() singleton and the objects it holds, the data-store and CRUD layer, and how the cart and session are assembled per visitor."},"1092":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-1","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"Bootstrap: from plugin file to `WC()`"},"1093":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-2","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"The `WC()` singleton"},"1094":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-3","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-data-layer-crud-classes-and-data-stores","content":"The data layer: CRUD classes and data stores"},"1095":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-4","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#sessions","content":"Sessions"},"1096":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#classic-and-blocks-are-two-front-ends-on-one-core","content":"Classic and Blocks are two front-ends on one core"},"1097":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#related","content":"Related"},"1098":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","content":"WooCommerce is a large plugin with a deliberate internal shape. Once you can\nname its main runtime objects and how they are wired together, reading core\nsource — and predicting where your own code should hook — gets much easier."},"1099":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","content":"This page is the architectural overview. Individual subsystems (cart totals,\ncheckout, orders, payments) get their own Architecture\npages in later phases."},"1100":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"WooCommerce loads like any plugin — its main file runs during the \"active\nplugins load\" step of the WordPress request lifecycle.\nFrom there it follows a defined sequence:"},"1101":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"WooCommerce fires its own actions during this sequence so extensions can hook\nthe right moment:"},"1102":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"Hook"},"1103":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"Fires"},"1104":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-13","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"Use it for"},"1105":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-14","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"`woocommerce_loaded`"},"1106":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-15","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"On WordPress `plugins_loaded`, priority `-1` — after every plugin is loaded, before WordPress `init`"},"1107":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-16","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"Code that needs WooCommerce's classes/functions to exist but must run before `init`"},"1108":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-17","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"`before_woocommerce_init`"},"1109":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-18","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"At the start of `WooCommerce::init()` (on WordPress `init`, priority 0)"},"1110":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-19","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"Declaring feature compatibility — HPOS, Cart/Checkout Blocks"},"1111":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-20","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"`woocommerce_init`"},"1112":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-21","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"At the end of `WooCommerce::init()`, same tick"},"1113":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-22","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"Most integration setup — factories, post types, and the session now exist"},"1114":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-23","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"`init` (WordPress, priority > 0)"},"1115":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-24","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"After `WooCommerce::init()` has run"},"1116":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-25","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"Anything depending on the `product` post type or WooCommerce taxonomies"},"1117":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-26","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"Declare feature compatibility from a callback on\nbefore\\_woocommerce\\_init:"},"1118":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-27","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#bootstrap-from-plugin-file-to-wc","content":"The feature slugs are custom\\_order\\_tables (HPOS) and\ncart\\_checkout\\_blocks. Declaring later has no effect — the plugin\nshows as \"incompatible\" and blocks the merchant from enabling the feature."},"1119":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-28","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"`WC()` is a global accessor that returns the one WooCommerce instance. It is\nthe entry point to the main runtime objects:"},"1120":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-29","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"Accessor"},"1121":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-30","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"Is"},"1122":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-31","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wooc