-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"`WC_Emails`"},"1146":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-55","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"The transactional email system"},"1147":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-56","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"`WC()->payment_gateways()` (method)"},"1148":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-57","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"`WC_Payment_Gateways`"},"1149":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-58","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"Registry of payment gateways"},"1150":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-59","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"`WC()->shipping()` (method)"},"1151":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-60","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"`WC_Shipping`"},"1152":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-61","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"Shipping method / zone registry and package calculation"},"1153":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-62","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"`WC()->queue()` (method)"},"1154":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-63","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"Action Scheduler proxy"},"1155":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-64","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"Schedule background jobs"},"1156":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-65","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-wc-singleton","content":"`WC()->cart` and `WC()->session` are **context-sensitive**. On admin, cron,\nand many REST requests they are `null` or empty because there is no visitor\nsession — `WooCommerce::init()` only calls `initialize_cart()` on front-end\nrequests. Code that assumes a cart always exists breaks when it runs in the\nwrong context."},"1157":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-66","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-data-layer-crud-classes-and-data-stores","content":"Since WooCommerce 3.0, stored entities are accessed through a two-part\npattern that deliberately hides *where* the data physically lives:"},"1158":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-67","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-data-layer-crud-classes-and-data-stores","content":"The practical rules:"},"1159":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-68","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-data-layer-crud-classes-and-data-stores","content":"Read and write WooCommerce entities through their CRUD class:\nwc\\_get\\_product( $id ), wc\\_get\\_order( $id ),\nnew WC\\_Customer( $id ). Call ->save() once after\nsetting values. This stays correct across HPOS and future storage changes."},"1160":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-69","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#the-data-layer-crud-classes-and-data-stores","content":"Writing directly to wp\\_postmeta for orders, or assuming a\nspecific table layout. Under HPOS the write goes to the wrong place or is\nsilently ignored, and reports/emails then disagree with the database."},"1161":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-70","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#sessions","content":"For anything that must persist across requests but is not a user account —\nthe guest cart, applied coupons, chosen shipping method, checkout progress —\nWooCommerce uses its own **session**, separate from PHP sessions."},"1162":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-71","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#sessions","content":"11.0.1 moved guest session cookies to a stronger, salted hashing scheme\n(with backward compatibility for existing cookies). The table name and the\n`woocommerce_cleanup_sessions` schedule are unchanged."},"1163":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-72","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#sessions","content":"Full-page caching and sessions interact badly if misconfigured: a cached\npage can show one visitor's cart count to another. Hosts and caching plugins\nnormally exclude cart/checkout/account pages and vary on the session cookie.\nThis gets a full treatment in the Performance section &#x2A;(planned)*."},"1164":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-73","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#classic-and-blocks-are-two-front-ends-on-one-core","content":"A recurring architectural fact: the **data and business logic layer is\nshared**, but the storefront presentation exists in two implementations."},"1165":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-74","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#classic-and-blocks-are-two-front-ends-on-one-core","content":"Both ultimately call the same `WC()->cart`, the same totals calculation, and\nthe same order-creation code. The split is at the edge, not the core — which\nis why \"change the value in core logic, change the presentation per\nfront-end\" is the reliable customization strategy."},"1166":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-75","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#classic-and-blocks-are-two-front-ends-on-one-core","content":"Since WooCommerce 8.3 the **Cart, Checkout, and Order Confirmation Blocks are\nthe default** on new installs. Stores created before 8.3 keep the classic\nshortcode pages until a merchant migrates them (WooCommerce → Status → Tools).\nSo a given store can be on either front-end — never assume."},"1167":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-76","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#related","content":"<Card title=\"WordPress Fundamentals\" href=\"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals\" description=\"The request lifecycle and hook system this bootstrap plugs into.\" />"},"1168":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-77","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#related","content":"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Data Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model\" description=\"The entities the CRUD layer manages and where each is stored.\" />"},"1169":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture-78","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture#related","content":"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Extension Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/extension-model\" description=\"Hooks, filters, templates, and blocks as one composable system.\" />"},"1170":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","type":"page","content":"WooCommerce Data Model","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model"},"1171":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-0","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","content":"The core entities WooCommerce manages — products and variations, orders and order items, customers, coupons — what each one is, how they relate, and which storage each lives in across classic and HPOS."},"1172":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-1","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"The entities at a glance"},"1173":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-2","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#products","content":"Products"},"1174":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-3","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#orders-and-order-items","content":"Orders and order items"},"1175":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-4","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#classic-vs-hpos-storage","content":"Classic vs HPOS storage"},"1176":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-5","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#customers","content":"Customers"},"1177":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-6","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#coupons","content":"Coupons"},"1178":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-7","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#how-the-entities-relate","content":"How the entities relate"},"1179":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-8","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#reading-the-model-correctly--summary","content":"Reading the model correctly — summary"},"1180":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-9","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#related","content":"Related"},"1181":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-10","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","content":"WooCommerce's data model is a commerce domain expressed in WordPress's\nstorage. Some entities are custom post types; some are custom tables; order\nstorage is currently mid-migration between the two. This page is the map."},"1182":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-11","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","content":"Read WooCommerce Architecture\nfirst if you have not — the CRUD-class-over-data-store pattern is what makes\nthis model workable."},"1183":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-12","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Entity"},"1184":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-13","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"CRUD class"},"1185":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-14","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Storage"},"1186":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-15","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Product"},"1187":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-16","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"`WC_Product` + `WC_Product_Simple` / `WC_Product_Variable` / `WC_Product_Grouped` / `WC_Product_External`"},"1188":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-17","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Post type `product`"},"1189":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-18","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Product variation"},"1190":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-19","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"`WC_Product_Variation`"},"1191":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-20","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Post type `product_variation`, child of a `product`"},"1192":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-21","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Order"},"1193":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-22","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"`WC_Order` (extends `WC_Abstract_Order`)"},"1194":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-23","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"HPOS: `wc_order*` tables. Legacy: post type `shop_order`"},"1195":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-24","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Order item"},"1196":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-25","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"`WC_Order_Item_Product` / `_Shipping` / `_Fee` / `_Coupon` / `_Tax` (extend `WC_Order_Item`)"},"1197":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-26","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"`woocommerce_order_items` + `woocommerce_order_itemmeta`"},"1198":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-27","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Refund"},"1199":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-28","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"`WC_Order_Refund`"},"1200":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-29","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Like an order; post type `shop_order_refund` in legacy mode"},"1201":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-30","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Customer"},"1202":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-31","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"`WC_Customer`"},"1203":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-32","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"WP user with role `customer`, or a guest (session + order only)"},"1204":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-33","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Coupon"},"1205":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-34","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"`WC_Coupon`"},"1206":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-35","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"Post type `shop_coupon`"},"1207":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-36","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#the-entities-at-a-glance","content":"All the product and order classes ultimately extend `WC_Data`, the base class\nthat provides the getter/setter/`save()` contract and delegates persistence to\na data store."},"1208":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-37","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#products","content":"A product is the most WordPress-shaped entity: a `product` post plus a lot of\nmeta plus taxonomy terms."},"1209":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-38","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#products","content":"Product **types** are set by the `product_type` taxonomy term on the product\n(`public => false`, `hierarchical => false&#x60;). The built-in terms are\n&#x2A;*`simple`*&#x2A;, &#x2A;*`variable`*&#x2A;, &#x2A;*`grouped`*&#x2A;, and &#x2A;*`external`** (external /\naffiliate); each maps to a `WC_Product_*` subclass. Extensions register more\n(`subscription`, `bundle`, `composite`, …) by adding a term and filtering the\nclass map (`woocommerce_product_class` / `woocommerce_product_type_query`)."},"1210":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-39","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#products","content":"$product = wc\\_get\\_product( $id ); then\n$product->get\\_price(), ->get\\_stock\\_quantity(),\n->is\\_in\\_stock(). The getters read from the right place\n(lookup table, meta, or computed) — raw meta reads do not."},"1211":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-40","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#orders-and-order-items","content":"An order is a container; the money and the goods live in its **items**. Even\nunder classic storage, order items were never post meta — they have always\nbeen in dedicated tables."},"1212":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-41","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#classic-vs-hpos-storage","content":"HPOS (\"High-Performance Order Storage\") settings offer three states:\n&#x2A;*\"WordPress post tables\"*&#x2A; (legacy), &#x2A;*\"High-performance order storage\"**,\nand legacy &#x2A;*with \"compatibility mode\"** enabled, which syncs writes to both.\nHPOS has been the default for **new** installs since WooCommerce 8.2;\npre-8.2 stores stay on post tables until migrated. Code that must work\neverywhere reads and writes only through `wc_get_order()` / `WC_Order`,\nqueries only through `wc_get_orders()`, and never runs `WP_Query` or direct\nSQL against a hard-coded order table. Internally,\n`WC_Data_Store::load( 'order' )` returns `OrdersTableDataStore` or\n`WC_Order_Data_Store_CPT` depending on which tables are authoritative. HPOS\ngets its own section in a later phase."},"1213":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-42","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#customers","content":"\"Customer\" is two things wearing one CRUD class:"},"1214":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-43","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#customers","content":"A WordPress user with role `customer` (capabilities: `read` plus\nWooCommerce's own `read_private_shop_orders` etc. for their own data),\nplus user meta for billing/shipping address, plus a row in\n`wp_wc_customer_lookup` for Analytics. Order history is every order with\ntheir `customer_id`."},"1215":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-44","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#customers","content":"No user row. The customer exists only as the address copied *onto the\norder*, plus a transient `WC_Customer` built from the session during\ncheckout. Analytics still gets a `wp_wc_customer_lookup` row, keyed by\nemail with `user_id = 0`, so guest orders are attributed."},"1216":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-45","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#customers","content":"11.0 added **guest order claiming**: a logged-in customer can link past\nguest-checkout orders (matched by email, with email verification) to their\naccount, after which those orders show in their order history."},"1217":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-46","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#coupons","content":"A coupon is a `shop_coupon` post whose meta holds the rule. The\n`discount_type` is one of `percent`, `fixed_cart`, or `fixed_product`; other\nmeta keys include `coupon_amount`, `individual_use`, `usage_limit`,\n`usage_limit_per_user`, `limit_usage_to_x_items`, `date_expires`,\n`free_shipping`, `product_ids` / `exclude_product_ids`, `product_categories` /\n`exclude_product_categories`, `minimum_amount`, `maximum_amount`. `WC_Coupon`\nreads it; the cart totals pipeline applies it."},"1218":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-47","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#how-the-entities-relate","content":"Note what is **not** a database entity: the cart. It is session data\n(see Architecture → Sessions).\nIts full structure and the totals pipeline are documented in the Cart\nsection in a later phase."},"1219":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-48","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#related","content":"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Architecture\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture\" description=\"The CRUD / data-store layer that abstracts all of this storage.\" />"},"1220":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-49","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#related","content":"<Card title=\"WordPress Fundamentals\" href=\"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals\" description=\"Post types, meta, and options — the primitives this model is built from.\" />"},"1221":{"id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model-50","page_id":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model#related","content":"<Card title=\"Developer Mental Model\" href=\"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model\" description=\"Why a change to one entity ripples across the others.\" />"},"1222":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","type":"page","content":"WordPress Fundamentals","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Foundations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals"},"1223":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-0","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","content":"The WordPress mechanisms WooCommerce is built on — the request lifecycle, post types, metadata, options, the hook system, cron, and the REST API — framed by how WooCommerce uses each one."},"1224":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-1","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-request-lifecycle","content":"The request lifecycle"},"1225":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-2","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"Post types"},"1226":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-3","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#metadata","content":"Metadata"},"1227":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-4","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#options","content":"Options"},"1228":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-5","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#hooks-actions-and-filters","content":"Hooks: actions and filters"},"1229":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-6","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#cron-and-scheduled-work","content":"Cron and scheduled work"},"1230":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-7","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"The REST API"},"1231":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-8","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#how-this-maps-forward","content":"How this maps forward"},"1232":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-9","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#related","content":"Related"},"1233":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-10","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","content":"WooCommerce is a WordPress plugin. Every capability it has is either a\nWordPress mechanism it reuses or a mechanism it adds *in the shape WordPress\nexpects*. If you understand these seven WordPress subsystems, most of\nWooCommerce's structure stops being surprising."},"1234":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-11","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","content":"This page is a WooCommerce-oriented refresher, not a full WordPress course.\nEach section says what the mechanism is, then **how WooCommerce leans on it**."},"1235":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-12","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-request-lifecycle","content":"Every front-end WooCommerce page is a normal WordPress request. Nothing about\na cart or a checkout changes the boot sequence — WooCommerce just registers\ncallbacks at specific points in it."},"1236":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-13","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-request-lifecycle","content":"These WordPress action names (`plugins_loaded`, `setup_theme`,\n`after_setup_theme`, `init`, `wp_loaded`, `parse_request`, `wp`,\n`template_redirect`) are long-standing core API and fire in this order on a\nnormal front-end request. WooCommerce's own `init()` method is hooked to\nWordPress `init` at priority `0`; the exact internal sequence is in\nWooCommerce Architecture."},"1237":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-14","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"WordPress stores most editable content as rows in one table (`wp_posts`),\ndistinguished by a `post_type` column. `post` and `page` are built in;\nplugins register their own with `register_post_type()`."},"1238":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-15","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"WooCommerce registers several custom post types:"},"1239":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-16","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"Post type"},"1240":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-17","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"Represents"},"1241":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-18","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"Notes"},"1242":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-19","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"`product`"},"1243":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-20","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"A catalog product"},"1244":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-21","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"`public`, has archives, uses custom taxonomies"},"1245":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-22","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"`product_variation`"},"1246":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-23","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"One variation of a variable product"},"1247":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-24","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"Child of a `product`; not `public`, hidden from the admin list"},"1248":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-25","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"`shop_coupon`"},"1249":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-26","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"A coupon"},"1250":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-27","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"Not `public`; admin-only"},"1251":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-28","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"`shop_order`"},"1252":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-29","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"An order"},"1253":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-30","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"Registered for compatibility; **not** the storage under HPOS (see below)"},"1254":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-31","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"`shop_order_refund`"},"1255":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-32","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"A refund against an order"},"1256":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-33","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"Child of an order"},"1257":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-34","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"`shop_webhook`"},"1258":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-35","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"A REST API webhook subscription"},"1259":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-36","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"Internal"},"1260":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-37","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"WooCommerce also registers taxonomies attached to `product`: `product_cat`\nand `product_tag` (the visible catalog taxonomies), `product_type` and\n`product_visibility` (internal, `public => false`, `hierarchical => false`),\nand one taxonomy per global attribute, named `pa_<attribute>` (e.g.\n`pa_color`)."},"1261":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-38","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#post-types","content":"**Orders are the exception.** With High-Performance Order Storage (HPOS)\nenabled, orders and refunds are stored in dedicated tables, not as\n`shop_order&#x60; posts. Treating an order as \"just a post\" is the single most\ncommon outdated assumption in older WooCommerce tutorials. See the HPOS\nsection &#x2A;(planned)* and\nWooCommerce Data Model."},"1262":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-39","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#metadata","content":"Alongside each post, WordPress keeps arbitrary key/value pairs in\n`wp_postmeta` (`post_id`, `meta_key`, `meta_value`), read with\n`get_post_meta()`. It is schemaless and flexible, and expensive to query at\nscale because `meta_value` is a long text column with no useful index."},"1263":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-40","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#metadata","content":"How WooCommerce uses it:"},"1264":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-41","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#metadata","content":"**Product data** — almost every product field is post meta under an\nunderscore-prefixed key: `_regular_price`, `_sale_price`, `_price`, `_sku`,\n`_stock`, `_stock_status`, `_weight`, `_length` / `_width` / `_height`,\n`_tax_class`, `_manage_stock`, `_downloadable`, `_virtual`, and more."},"1265":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-42","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#metadata","content":"**Lookup tables** — because meta queries are slow, WooCommerce maintains\n`wp_wc_product_meta_lookup` (added in WooCommerce 3.7): one row per product\nwith real columns for `sku`, `min_price` / `max_price`, `stock_status`,\n`stock_quantity`, `onsale`, `rating_count`, `average_rating`, `total_sales`,\n`virtual`, `downloadable`, `tax_status`, `tax_class`. Catalog queries and\nsorting hit this table instead of `wp_postmeta`, and WooCommerce keeps it in\nsync on save."},"1266":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-43","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#metadata","content":"**CRUD abstraction** — you are encouraged to read product and order data\nthrough `WC_Product` / `WC_Order` getter methods, not `get_post_meta()`\ndirectly, so that HPOS and lookup tables stay correct. This is covered in\nWooCommerce Data Model."},"1267":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-44","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#metadata","content":"Reading WooCommerce data with get\\_post\\_meta() works today for\nproducts but bypasses the data-store layer. For orders under HPOS it can\nreturn stale data or nothing. Prefer the CRUD getters."},"1268":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-45","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#options","content":"`wp_options` holds site-wide settings as key/value rows, read with\n`get_option()`. Rows flagged `autoload = yes` are **all loaded on every\nrequest** into memory. A bloated autoload set is a classic WordPress\nperformance problem."},"1269":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-46","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#options","content":"WooCommerce uses options for essentially all store configuration — pages,\ncurrency, tax behavior, checkout options, email settings, gateway settings —\nmostly under a `woocommerce_` key prefix (for example `woocommerce_currency`,\n`woocommerce_cart_page_id`, `woocommerce_calc_taxes`,\n`woocommerce_default_country`). Many are autoloaded; the store's own settings\nplus each active extension's settings all add to the per-request autoload\npayload."},"1270":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-47","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#options","content":"When the Performance section &#x2A;(planned)* is written, autoloaded option\nweight from WooCommerce and its extensions gets its own treatment —\nit is one of the highest-leverage things to audit on a slow store."},"1271":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-48","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#hooks-actions-and-filters","content":"The hook system is how WordPress code is changed without editing it. Two\nkinds:"},"1272":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-49","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#hooks-actions-and-filters","content":"Both share the same mechanics: callbacks register with a **priority** (lower\nruns earlier, default 10) and a declared number of **accepted arguments**.\nWooCommerce exposes hundreds of each. The distinction matters:"},"1273":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-50","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#hooks-actions-and-filters","content":"Want to *add markup* next to the price? An **action** at that position."},"1274":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-51","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#hooks-actions-and-filters","content":"Want to *change the price value*? A **filter** on the value."},"1275":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-52","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#hooks-actions-and-filters","content":"Putting display logic in a value filter, or trying to change a value from an\naction, is a frequent source of \"my code runs but nothing changes\"."},"1276":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-53","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#hooks-actions-and-filters","content":"Hook *names* are the most version-sensitive API surface in WooCommerce.\nSpecific hooks named across the Foundations pages have been checked against\nWooCommerce 11.0.1; anything still unverified carries a &#xNAN; tag.\nThe Development section &#x2A;(planned)* documents hook discovery and debugging in\ndepth."},"1277":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-54","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#cron-and-scheduled-work","content":"WordPress has \"cron\" (`wp_schedule_event()`, the `wp_cron` option) that runs\ndue tasks on regular page loads — not a real system cron unless wired to one.\nIt is fine for light, non-urgent work and unreliable for anything precise or\nhigh-volume."},"1278":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-55","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#cron-and-scheduled-work","content":"WooCommerce bundles **Action Scheduler**, a more robust queue built on top of\nWordPress. Since Action Scheduler 3.0 it stores jobs in its own tables —\n`wp_actionscheduler_actions`, `wp_actionscheduler_logs`,\n`wp_actionscheduler_groups`, `wp_actionscheduler_claims` — processes them in\nbatches on the `action_scheduler_run_queue` hook (dispatched roughly once a\nminute via WP-Cron), and retries failures. WooCommerce and many extensions\nuse it for deferred emails, webhook delivery, analytics/report generation,\nand data migrations including the HPOS backfill."},"1279":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-56","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#cron-and-scheduled-work","content":"Two behaviour changes to know if you schedule your own jobs: unique-action\nchecks now include the action's **arguments** (previously hook + group only),\nso more actions can be created than before; and failed actions are now\nauto-purged after \\~3 months (`action_scheduler_retention_period_for_failed`,\ndisable via `action_scheduler_enable_failed_action_cleanup`)."},"1280":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-57","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#cron-and-scheduled-work","content":"For your own deferred work in a WooCommerce context, schedule it through\nAction Scheduler rather than raw wp\\_schedule\\_single\\_event() —\nyou get batching, retries, and an admin view of the queue."},"1281":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-58","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"WordPress ships a REST API under `/wp-json/`. WooCommerce adds two distinct\nAPI surfaces on top:"},"1282":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-59","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"API"},"1283":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-60","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"Base route"},"1284":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-61","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"Purpose"},"1285":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-62","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"Auth"},"1286":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-63","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"WooCommerce REST API"},"1287":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-64","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"`/wp-json/wc/v3/`"},"1288":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-65","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"Server-to-server: `products`, `orders`, `customers`, `coupons`, `products/reviews`, `reports`, `system_status`, settings, webhooks"},"1289":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-66","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"API keys (consumer key/secret) or cookie auth + nonce"},"1290":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-67","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"Store API"},"1291":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-68","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"`/wp-json/wc/store/v1/`"},"1292":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-69","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"Front-end: `cart`, `cart/items`, `cart/coupons`, `checkout`, `products`, `products/collection-data` — drives the Cart/Checkout Blocks and headless"},"1293":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-70","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"Cart token / nonce; designed for the browser, no API keys"},"1294":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-71","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#the-rest-api","content":"The two are not interchangeable. `wc/v3` is an admin/integration tool with\nfull CRUD on stored records. The Store API is a customer-facing surface that\nmanages a *session cart* and drives the Cart and Checkout Blocks; it is\nversioned separately (`v1`) and is not a drop-in for `wc/v3`. Both get their\nown pages in later phases (Development section, *planned*)."},"1295":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-72","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#related","content":"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Architecture\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture\" description=\"How WooCommerce boots on top of this lifecycle and organizes itself in memory.\" />"},"1296":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-73","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#related","content":"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Data Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model\" description=\"What WooCommerce stores, in which tables, and how to read it correctly.\" />"},"1297":{"id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals-74","page_id":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals#related","content":"<Card title=\"Why WooCommerce?\" href=\"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce\" description=\"What WooCommerce adds to the WordPress base described here.\" />"},"1298":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","type":"page","content":"Developer Mental Model","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Introduction"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model"},"1299":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-0","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","content":"Building on WooCommerce is not building a brochure or blog site. This chapter introduces the dimensions a WooCommerce developer has to think in, and how one small change ripples through the system."},"1300":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-1","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#a-blog-site-is-one-dimension-a-store-is-several","content":"A blog site is one dimension. A store is several."},"1301":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-2","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#the-question-is-not-how-do-i-change-the-output","content":"The question is not \"how do I change the output\""},"1302":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-3","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#one-change-ripples","content":"One change ripples"},"1303":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-4","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#three-layers-of-where-a-change-belongs","content":"Three layers of \"where a change belongs\""},"1304":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-5","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#think-in-the-lifecycle-not-the-page","content":"Think in the lifecycle, not the page"},"1305":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-6","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#what-this-means-in-practice","content":"What this means in practice"},"1306":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-7","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#do-not-over-learn-this-yet","content":"Do not over-learn this yet"},"1307":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-8","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#related","content":"Related"},"1308":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-9","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","content":"If your background is WordPress themes and content sites, WooCommerce will\nfeel deceptively familiar — same admin, same hooks, same templates — and then\nsuddenly unfamiliar the moment you touch anything commerce-related. This\nchapter is about the shift in thinking that closes that gap."},"1309":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-10","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","content":"We introduce the idea here and link outward. Later steps of WooDoc expand\neach layer in depth."},"1310":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-11","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#a-blog-site-is-one-dimension-a-store-is-several","content":"On a brochure or blog site, most work is **one-dimensional**: content goes in,\nmarkup comes out. Change the template, change the output."},"1311":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-12","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#a-blog-site-is-one-dimension-a-store-is-several","content":"A store forces you to think in **multiple dimensions at once**, because a\nsingle visible thing is the result of business rules, a lifecycle, data, and\noften an external service:"},"1312":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-13","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#the-question-is-not-how-do-i-change-the-output","content":"A theme developer asks:"},"1313":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-14","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#the-question-is-not-how-do-i-change-the-output","content":"> \"How do I change the displayed price?\""},"1314":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-15","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#the-question-is-not-how-do-i-change-the-output","content":"A WooCommerce developer eventually learns to ask:"},"1315":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-16","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#the-question-is-not-how-do-i-change-the-output","content":"Because in WooCommerce, \"the price\" is not one thing in one place."},"1316":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-17","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#one-change-ripples","content":"Suppose you change a product's price. Here is the chain of things that can\ndepend on that value:"},"1317":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-18","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#one-change-ripples","content":"Overriding the price in the template changes the *number on the screen* but\nnot the *number WooCommerce calculates with*. The customer sees one price and\nis charged another. The correct layer for a value change is a pricing filter\nor the cart calculation stage — not the display template."},"1318":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-19","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#one-change-ripples","content":"Concretely: the catalog price a product reports is filtered by\n`woocommerce_product_get_price` (and `_get_regular_price` /\n`_get_sale_price`); the formatted catalog price HTML by\n`woocommerce_get_price_html`. The amount a cart line is *charged* is set by\ncalling `set_price()` on the line's product object during\n`woocommerce_before_calculate_totals` — `woocommerce_cart_item_price` only\nchanges what is *displayed*. Confusing the two is exactly the bug above."},"1319":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-20","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#three-layers-of-where-a-change-belongs","content":"Every customization sits at one of three safety levels. WooDoc labels them\nconsistently:"},"1320":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-21","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#three-layers-of-where-a-change-belongs","content":"**Recommended extension** — official hooks, filters, and APIs; supported\ntemplate mechanisms; a properly structured plugin or `mu-plugin`. Survives\nupdates. This is the default answer."},"1321":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-22","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#three-layers-of-where-a-change-belongs","content":"**Possible but risky** — overriding a template by copying it into your\ntheme, or replacing a whole subsystem. Sometimes the right call, but you now\nown that copy forever and must re-check it on every WooCommerce update."},"1322":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-23","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#three-layers-of-where-a-change-belongs","content":"**Dangerous** — editing WooCommerce core files, or depending on private\ninternal behavior that has no stability guarantee. Breaks on update, breaks\nsilently, and breaks other people's expectations."},"1323":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-24","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#three-layers-of-where-a-change-belongs","content":"You will see these three labels throughout WooDoc. The recurring lesson:"},"1324":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-25","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#three-layers-of-where-a-change-belongs","content":"> **\"Just because I can change it there does not mean I should.\"**"},"1325":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-26","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#think-in-the-lifecycle-not-the-page","content":"A brochure site has pages. WooCommerce has a **lifecycle** that pages are\nwindows into:"},"1326":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-27","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#think-in-the-lifecycle-not-the-page","content":"When something behaves unexpectedly, the first diagnostic question is usually\n*which stage of this lifecycle am I in, and what code runs at that stage* —\nnot *which template rendered this*."},"1327":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-28","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#what-this-means-in-practice","content":"**Locate before you edit.** Identify the layer and lifecycle stage first.\nThe Where Does This Come From?\npattern is built for exactly this."},"1328":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-29","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#what-this-means-in-practice","content":"**Change values at the calculation layer, formatting at the display layer.**\nDo not confuse the two."},"1329":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-30","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#what-this-means-in-practice","content":"**Prefer the highest-safety layer that can do the job.** Hook or filter\nfirst; template override only when a hook cannot reach it; never core."},"1330":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-31","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#what-this-means-in-practice","content":"**Trace the ripple.** Before shipping, list what downstream steps your\nchange affects and confirm each still behaves."},"1331":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-32","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#what-this-means-in-practice","content":"**Respect classic vs Blocks.** The same customization can require different\ntechniques depending on which cart/checkout implementation is active."},"1332":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-33","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#do-not-over-learn-this-yet","content":"You do not need to memorize the full lifecycle now. The goal of this chapter\nis only to install the *shape* of the problem:"},"1333":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-34","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#do-not-over-learn-this-yet","content":"> WooCommerce work is multi-dimensional. A change has a **layer**, a\n> **lifecycle stage**, a **safety level**, and a **ripple**. Name all four\n> before you write code."},"1334":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-35","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#do-not-over-learn-this-yet","content":"Later steps of WooDoc document each stage — cart calculation, checkout,\norder lifecycle, payment flow, email flow — in detail."},"1335":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-36","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#related","content":"<Card title=\"Where Does This Come From?\" href=\"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from\" description=\"The step-by-step pattern for locating any WooCommerce element.\" />"},"1336":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-37","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#related","content":"<Card title=\"Why WooCommerce?\" href=\"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce\" description=\"The trade-offs you are working within.\" />"},"1337":{"id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model-38","page_id":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model#related","content":"<Card title=\"Roadmap\" href=\"/docs/about/roadmap\" description=\"Where each lifecycle stage gets documented in depth.\" />"},"1338":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","type":"page","content":"Where Does This Come From?","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Introduction"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from"},"1339":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-0","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","content":"WooDoc's signature pattern for tracing any WooCommerce element back to the layer that produced it — and deciding where it is safe to change."},"1340":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-1","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#the-five-questions","content":"The five questions"},"1341":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-2","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#walking-each-question","content":"Walking each question"},"1342":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-3","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#1-what-am-i-looking-at","content":"1\\. What am I looking at?"},"1343":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-4","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#2-where-does-it-come-from","content":"2\\. Where does it come from?"},"1344":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-5","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#3-what-controls-it","content":"3\\. What controls it?"},"1345":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-6","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#4-what-can-i-safely-modify","content":"4\\. What can I safely modify?"},"1346":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-7","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#5-what-should-i-avoid","content":"5\\. What should I avoid?"},"1347":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-8","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#worked-shape-illustrative","content":"Worked shape (illustrative)"},"1348":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-9","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#why-this-pattern-matters","content":"Why this pattern matters"},"1349":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-10","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#related","content":"Related"},"1350":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-11","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","content":"This is the pattern WooDoc is built around. When you see any WooCommerce\nelement — a button, a field, a line of totals, a message, an email — you\nshould be able to walk a short, repeatable path from &#x2A;\"what is this?\"&#x2A; to\n&#x2A;\"where do I safely change it?\"*."},"1351":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-12","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","content":"Later steps of WooDoc apply this pattern to concrete elements (the add-to-cart\nbutton, checkout fields, order-status emails, and so on). This page teaches\nthe pattern itself."},"1352":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-13","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#1-what-am-i-looking-at","content":"Name the element precisely. \"The price\" is ambiguous; \"the sale price shown on\nthe single product page\" is not. Is it text, a form control, a link, a\ncomputed value, a status message?"},"1353":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-14","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#2-where-does-it-come-from","content":"Identify the **layer** that emitted it:"},"1354":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-15","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#2-where-does-it-come-from","content":"Practical tells: view source vs. inspect the live DOM (a difference means JS or\nAJAX built it); search the WooCommerce `templates/` directory for visible\nstatic text; check whether the value changes without a full page reload\n(fragments / Blocks)."},"1355":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-16","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#3-what-controls-it","content":"Once you know the layer, find the specific control point: the template file and\nthe hook fired inside it, the filter applied to the value, the block and its\nsettings, or the script and the endpoint it calls."},"1356":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-17","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#4-what-can-i-safely-modify","content":"Map the control point to a **safety level**:"},"1357":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-18","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#4-what-can-i-safely-modify","content":"There is a hook or filter for exactly this. Use it from a plugin or\n`mu-plugin`. First choice, every time."},"1358":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-19","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#4-what-can-i-safely-modify","content":"No hook reaches it, but the template can be overridden in your theme, or a\nblock exposes a Slot/Fill. Acceptable — record that you now maintain that\noverride against future WooCommerce updates."},"1359":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-20","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#4-what-can-i-safely-modify","content":"The only way to change it is editing a core file or relying on an internal\nthat has no stability promise. Stop and find another approach."},"1360":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-21","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#5-what-should-i-avoid","content":"State the thing not to do and why: do not edit the core template in place; do\nnot change the displayed value without changing the calculated value; do not\nhook a stage that does not fire under the active cart/checkout implementation."},"1361":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-22","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#worked-shape-illustrative","content":"The concrete file paths, hook names, and script handles referenced across\nWooDoc are being verified against this version. Anything not yet confirmed is\nmarked with a  tag."},"1362":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-23","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#why-this-pattern-matters","content":"It converts \"WooCommerce is a black box\" into a **finite lookup**. You are\nnever guessing — you are walking layers from output back to source, and\nstopping at the safest one that can do the job."},"1363":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-24","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#related","content":"<Card title=\"Developer Mental Model\" href=\"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model\" description=\"The layers, lifecycle, safety levels, and ripple this pattern draws on.\" />"},"1364":{"id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from-25","page_id":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from#related","content":"<Card title=\"Documentation Design System\" href=\"/docs/about/design-system\" description=\"The page templates and components that encode this pattern.\" />"},"1365":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"page","content":"Why WooCommerce?","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Introduction"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce"},"1366":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-0","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","content":"What problem WooCommerce solves, why WordPress alone is not an e-commerce platform, what WooCommerce adds, the trade-offs of choosing it, and when it is the wrong tool."},"1367":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-1","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#the-short-version","content":"The short version"},"1368":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-2","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-wordpress-alone-is-not-an-e-commerce-platform","content":"Why WordPress alone is not an e-commerce platform"},"1369":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-3","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"What WooCommerce adds"},"1370":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-4","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-provides-out-of-the-box","content":"What WooCommerce provides out of the box"},"1371":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-5","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-businesses-choose-woocommerce","content":"Why businesses choose WooCommerce"},"1372":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-6","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-developers-choose-woocommerce","content":"Why developers choose WooCommerce"},"1373":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-7","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#the-trade-offs","content":"The trade-offs"},"1374":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-8","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#where-woocommerce-fits-compared-with-a-custom-application","content":"Where WooCommerce fits compared with a custom application"},"1375":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-9","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-is-a-good-choice","content":"When WooCommerce is a good choice"},"1376":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-10","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-may-not-be-a-good-choice","content":"When WooCommerce may not be a good choice"},"1377":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-11","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#key-takeaways","content":"Key takeaways"},"1378":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-12","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#related","content":"Related"},"1379":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-13","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","content":"Before learning how WooCommerce works, it is worth being clear about **why it\nexists** and **why you would choose it**. This chapter is not a sales pitch.\nThe goal is to establish the reason for WooCommerce before teaching its\nmechanics — and to be honest about where it fits and where it does not."},"1380":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-14","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#the-short-version","content":"WordPress is a content management system. It manages *pages of content* and\nthe people who edit them. It has no concept of a product, a price, a cart, an\norder, a customer, tax, shipping, or a payment."},"1381":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-15","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#the-short-version","content":"**WooCommerce is the layer that adds all of that** — a commerce domain model,\na checkout pipeline, an order lifecycle, and the extension points to change\nevery part of it — while reusing WordPress's users, content, admin, hooks,\nREST API, and plugin ecosystem."},"1382":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-16","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-wordpress-alone-is-not-an-e-commerce-platform","content":"A WordPress install gives you:"},"1383":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-17","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-wordpress-alone-is-not-an-e-commerce-platform","content":"**Posts and pages** — arbitrary content, stored in `wp_posts`."},"1384":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-18","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-wordpress-alone-is-not-an-e-commerce-platform","content":"**Users and roles** — accounts and capabilities."},"1385":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-19","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-wordpress-alone-is-not-an-e-commerce-platform","content":"**Options** — site-wide settings."},"1386":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-20","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-wordpress-alone-is-not-an-e-commerce-platform","content":"**Taxonomies** — categories and tags."},"1387":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-21","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-wordpress-alone-is-not-an-e-commerce-platform","content":"**Hooks and filters** — a way to change behavior without editing core."},"1388":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-22","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-wordpress-alone-is-not-an-e-commerce-platform","content":"**A REST API and a cron system.**"},"1389":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-23","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-wordpress-alone-is-not-an-e-commerce-platform","content":"None of that is commerce. To sell something you need concepts WordPress simply\ndoes not have:"},"1390":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-24","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-wordpress-alone-is-not-an-e-commerce-platform","content":"You could build this yourself as a custom plugin. WooCommerce is that plugin —\nmature, widely deployed, and with a large extension ecosystem."},"1391":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-25","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"On top of WordPress, WooCommerce provides:"},"1392":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-26","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"Area"},"1393":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-27","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"What you get"},"1394":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-28","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**Data model**"},"1395":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-29","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"Products (simple, variable, grouped, external), product variations, coupons, orders, order items, customers, refunds — each with CRUD classes and pluggable data stores."},"1396":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-30","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**Storefront**"},"1397":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-31","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"Shop, product, cart, checkout, and account pages, rendered through classic PHP templates *or* WooCommerce Blocks."},"1398":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-32","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**Cart & session**"},"1399":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-33","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"A per-visitor cart, session persistence for guests and logged-in users, and AJAX cart fragments."},"1400":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-34","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**Totals engine**"},"1401":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-35","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"An ordered calculation of line totals, discounts, fees, tax, and shipping."},"1402":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-36","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**Checkout**"},"1403":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-37","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"Address fields, validation, payment method selection, order creation, and the \"thank you\" / order-received flow."},"1404":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-38","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**Order engine**"},"1405":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-39","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"Order statuses, status-transition hooks, stock reduction, and admin order management."},"1406":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-40","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**Payments & shipping**"},"1407":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-41","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"Built-in offline gateways (`bacs` direct bank transfer, `cheque`, `cod` cash on delivery) and shipping methods (`flat_rate`, `free_shipping`, `local_pickup`), plus a `WC_Payment_Gateway` / `WC_Shipping_Method` interface for adding more."},"1408":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-42","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**Tax**"},"1409":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-43","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"Tax classes, rates, and rules, with configurable rounding and display."},"1410":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-44","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**Emails**"},"1411":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-45","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"A templated transactional email system with per-email settings."},"1412":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-46","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**REST & Store API**"},"1413":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-47","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"`wc/v3` REST API (`products`, `orders`, `customers`, `coupons`, `reports`, …) and the separate `wc/store/v1` Store API for headless / block front-ends."},"1414":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-48","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**Admin**"},"1415":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-49","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"Settings screens, product editor, order screens, reports, and a status/system report."},"1416":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-50","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"**Extensibility**"},"1417":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-51","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-adds","content":"Hundreds of actions and filters, template overrides, and plugin-oriented architecture."},"1418":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-52","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-provides-out-of-the-box","content":"Without any extensions, a default WooCommerce install can:"},"1419":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-53","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-provides-out-of-the-box","content":"Sell physical, digital/downloadable, and simple \"external/affiliate\"\nproducts, including products with variations."},"1420":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-54","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-provides-out-of-the-box","content":"Take payment via the three built-in offline methods (direct bank transfer,\ncheque, cash on delivery). A live card gateway is a quick guided install\nduring onboarding (WooPayments / Stripe / PayPal), not bundled code —\nPayPal Standard was removed from core for new installs in WooCommerce 5.5."},"1421":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-55","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-provides-out-of-the-box","content":"Apply coupons, flat-rate and free shipping, and configurable tax."},"1422":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-56","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-provides-out-of-the-box","content":"Send transactional emails and manage orders through the admin."},"1423":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-57","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-provides-out-of-the-box","content":"Expose products and orders over a REST API."},"1424":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-58","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#what-woocommerce-provides-out-of-the-box","content":"What it does **not** do out of the box includes subscriptions, bookings,\nmemberships, multi-vendor marketplaces, advanced product configurators, deep\nERP/accounting integration, and many region-specific tax or invoicing\nrequirements. Those are extensions or custom development."},"1425":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-59","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-businesses-choose-woocommerce","content":"Content, marketing, and store live in one system, one admin, one hosting\nsetup, one skill set."},"1426":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-60","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-businesses-choose-woocommerce","content":"Editorial commerce, content-driven catalogs, and SEO-heavy stores benefit\nfrom WordPress's publishing tooling."},"1427":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-61","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-businesses-choose-woocommerce","content":"No platform revenue share; hosting and extensions are the main costs."},"1428":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-62","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-businesses-choose-woocommerce","content":"The extension ecosystem plus full code access means most requirements can\nbe met without leaving the platform."},"1429":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-63","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-developers-choose-woocommerce","content":"**It is open source and readable.** You can follow a request from URL to\ntemplate to hook to data store in actual source code."},"1430":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-64","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-developers-choose-woocommerce","content":"**It reuses WordPress skills.** Hooks, filters, the plugin model, WP-CLI,\nand the REST API all carry over."},"1431":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-65","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-developers-choose-woocommerce","content":"**Extension points are first-class.** Most behavior can be changed with an\naction or filter, without touching core or a template."},"1432":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-66","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-developers-choose-woocommerce","content":"**The ecosystem is large.** Payment, shipping, tax, and marketing\nintegrations usually already exist."},"1433":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-67","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#why-developers-choose-woocommerce","content":"**It scales down and up.** The same platform runs a hobby store and a\nhigh-traffic catalog (with real infrastructure work at the top end)."},"1434":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-68","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#the-trade-offs","content":"Choosing WooCommerce is choosing a set of constraints:"},"1435":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-69","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#the-trade-offs","content":"**You own the stack.** Hosting, performance, security patching, backups,\nand uptime are your responsibility, not a vendor's."},"1436":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-70","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#the-trade-offs","content":"**Plugin sprawl is a real risk.** Every extension is code running in your\nrequest path; conflicts and performance regressions come with the model."},"1437":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-71","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#the-trade-offs","content":"**The data model is WordPress-shaped.** Products are a custom post type;\nhistorically, orders were too. This is flexible but not what you would\ndesign from scratch for high-volume transactional data. HPOS\n(High-Performance Order Storage) addresses order storage specifically."},"1438":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-72","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#the-trade-offs","content":"**Performance requires deliberate work** at scale — object caching, a\ntuned host, careful extension choices, and sometimes a headless front-end."},"1439":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-73","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#the-trade-offs","content":"**\"Classic vs Blocks\" is a live migration.** Cart and Checkout exist in\ntwo implementations, and customization advice differs between them."},"1440":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-74","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#the-trade-offs","content":"Display and checkout-processing hooks from the classic flow do **not** run\nunder the Checkout Block — including `woocommerce_checkout_fields`,\n`woocommerce_before_checkout_form`,\n`woocommerce_checkout_before_customer_details`,\n`woocommerce_review_order_before_payment`, `woocommerce_checkout_create_order`,\nand `woocommerce_checkout_order_processed`. The block path fires Store API\nequivalents instead, such as\n`woocommerce_store_api_checkout_update_order_from_request` and\n`woocommerce_store_api_checkout_order_processed`. Order-object and\nstatus-transition hooks — `woocommerce_new_order`,\n`woocommerce_order_status_changed`, `woocommerce_thankyou` — still fire in\nboth."},"1441":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-75","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-is-a-good-choice","content":"The operational and skills overlap is decisive."},"1442":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-76","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-is-a-good-choice","content":"WordPress's publishing strength is a genuine advantage."},"1443":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-77","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-is-a-good-choice","content":"Standard retail, digital downloads, simple subscriptions, common shipping\nand tax setups."},"1444":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-78","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-is-a-good-choice","content":"No platform lock-in; full access to the database and the request lifecycle."},"1445":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-79","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-is-a-good-choice","content":"Comfortably within range for tuned single-site hosting."},"1446":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-80","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-may-not-be-a-good-choice","content":"A purpose-built system on a relational schema you control may be a better\nfit than a CMS-shaped model — evaluate carefully rather than assume."},"1447":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-81","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-may-not-be-a-good-choice","content":"Deep custom logic, real-time pricing, or B2B quoting can outgrow the\nproduct model and become most of your codebase anyway."},"1448":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-82","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-may-not-be-a-good-choice","content":"Possible with extensions, but the architecture fights you; a dedicated\nmarketplace stack may be cleaner."},"1449":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-83","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-may-not-be-a-good-choice","content":"If the app is a Laravel / Node / Rails product and checkout is one screen,\nembedding a payment provider directly is often simpler than adding\nWordPress."},"1450":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-84","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-may-not-be-a-good-choice","content":"Someone has to own hosting, updates, and security. Without that, a hosted\nplatform lowers risk."},"1451":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-85","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#when-woocommerce-may-not-be-a-good-choice","content":"WooDoc will not pretend WooCommerce is always the answer. A recurring theme in\nlater chapters is &#x2A;\"here is what this costs, here is where it strains, here is\nwhen to reach for something else.\"*"},"1452":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-86","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#key-takeaways","content":"WordPress manages content; **WooCommerce adds the entire commerce domain**\non top of it."},"1453":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-87","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#key-takeaways","content":"You choose WooCommerce for the **WordPress overlap, the ecosystem, and full\ncode ownership** — and you accept **operating the stack yourself**."},"1454":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-88","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#key-takeaways","content":"The **classic vs Blocks** split is the most important current caveat for\ndevelopers customizing the storefront."},"1455":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-89","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#key-takeaways","content":"It is an excellent fit for content-led, moderate-volume retail and a poor\nfit for very high-volume transactional systems or apps where commerce is a\nminor feature."},"1456":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-90","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#related","content":"<Card title=\"Developer Mental Model\" href=\"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model\" description=\"How to think when you build on WooCommerce instead of a blog.\" />"},"1457":{"id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce-91","page_id":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce#related","content":"<Card title=\"Where Does This Come From?\" href=\"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from\" description=\"Tracing any element back to the layer that produced it.\" />"},"1458":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","type":"page","content":"Cart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Commerce Lifecycle"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart"},"1459":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-0","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","content":"The cart subsystem — what the cart is (session data, not a table), the shape of a cart item, the totals calculation pipeline and its fixed order of operations, where coupons and fees apply, and how to change a line price correctly."},"1460":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-1","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"What the cart is"},"1461":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-2","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#the-totals-calculation-pipeline","content":"The totals calculation pipeline"},"1462":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-3","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#coupons","content":"Coupons"},"1463":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-4","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#fees","content":"Fees"},"1464":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-5","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#changing-a-line-price","content":"Changing a line price"},"1465":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-6","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#fragments","content":"Fragments"},"1466":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-7","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#classic-vs-blocks","content":"Classic vs Blocks"},"1467":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-8","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#related","content":"Related"},"1468":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-9","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","content":"The cart is the most misunderstood part of WooCommerce. It is **not a database\ntable** — it is per-visitor\nsession data that is\nrecalculated from scratch on almost every request. Understanding the\nrecalculation pipeline is the key to changing anything about pricing."},"1469":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-10","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"Each **cart item** is an array. The important keys:"},"1470":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-11","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"Key"},"1471":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-12","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"Holds"},"1472":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-13","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"`key`"},"1473":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-14","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"The cart item key — also the array key"},"1474":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-15","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"`product_id`, `variation_id`, `variation`"},"1475":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-16","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"What was added"},"1476":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-17","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"`quantity`"},"1477":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-18","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"How many"},"1478":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-19","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"`data`"},"1479":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-20","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"A live `WC_Product` object for this line — this is what pricing reads"},"1480":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-21","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"`data_hash`"},"1481":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-22","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"A hash of the product data, so a price change invalidates a stale session line"},"1482":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-23","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"`line_subtotal`, `line_subtotal_tax`, `line_total`, `line_tax`, `line_tax_data`"},"1483":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-24","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"Filled in by the totals pipeline, not by `add_to_cart()`"},"1484":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-25","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#what-the-cart-is","content":"The **cart item key** is `md5()` of the product id, variation id, variation\ndata, and any extra cart-item data, via `WC_Cart::generate_cart_id()` —\nfilterable with `woocommerce_cart_id`. Adding the same product with different\ncustom data (an engraving, a gift note) produces a different key and a\nseparate line."},"1485":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-26","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#the-totals-calculation-pipeline","content":"`WC()->cart->calculate_totals()` runs a **fixed sequence**. It fires\n`woocommerce_before_calculate_totals`, hands the cart to a `WC_Cart_Totals`\ninstance (the dedicated arithmetic class since WooCommerce 3.2), then fires\n`woocommerce_after_calculate_totals`."},"1486":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-27","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#the-totals-calculation-pipeline","content":"Because totals are recomputed every request, anything you change must be\nre-applied every time `calculate_totals()` runs — you cannot \"set it once\".\nHook the pipeline, don't patch a stored total."},"1487":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-28","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#coupons","content":"An applied coupon is stored in the session as a code. During calculation\n`WC_Discounts` loads each `WC_Coupon`, validates it against the current cart\n(usage limits, product/category restrictions, min/max spend, expiry), and\napplies the discount by `discount_type`\n(`percent` / `fixed_cart` / `fixed_product`)."},"1488":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-29","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#fees","content":"Fees are the sanctioned way to add a positive or negative amount to the cart\nthat is not a product line:"},"1489":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-30","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#fees","content":"A negative fee is how you apply a programmatic discount that a coupon cannot\nexpress."},"1490":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-31","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#changing-a-line-price","content":"The correct place is `woocommerce_before_calculate_totals` — set the price on\nthe line's product object, which the pipeline then uses for every subsequent\nstep (subtotal, tax, total):"},"1491":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-32","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#changing-a-line-price","content":"Filtering woocommerce\\_cart\\_item\\_price to show a different number\nchanges the display only. The customer is still charged the\ncalculated total. Value at the calculation layer, formatting at the display\nlayer — never confuse them."},"1492":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-33","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#fragments","content":"The mini-cart / cart-count refresh after AJAX add-to-cart is the **fragments**\nsystem — covered in\nJavaScript → cart fragments.\nIts background `get_refreshed_fragments` request has a real per-page cost on\nbusy stores."},"1493":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-34","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#related","content":"<Card title=\"Checkout\" href=\"/docs/lifecycle/checkout\" description=\"Where the calculated cart becomes an order.\" />"},"1494":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-35","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#related","content":"<Card title=\"Shipping & Tax\" href=\"/docs/lifecycle/shipping-and-tax\" description=\"Two stages of the totals pipeline in detail.\" />"},"1495":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart-36","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/cart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/cart#related","content":"<Card title=\"Developer Mental Model\" href=\"/docs/introduction/developer-mental-model\" description=\"Why one price change ripples through this whole pipeline.\" />"},"1496":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","type":"page","content":"Checkout","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Commerce Lifecycle"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout"},"1497":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-0","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","content":"The checkout subsystem — the WC_Checkout controller, where the field list comes from and how to change it, the validation pipeline, how an order is created from the cart, and how all of this differs between classic and the Checkout Block."},"1498":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-1","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#the-controller","content":"The controller"},"1499":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-2","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#where-the-field-list-comes-from","content":"Where the field list comes from"},"1500":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-3","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#validation","content":"Validation"},"1501":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-4","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#order-creation","content":"Order creation"},"1502":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-5","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#classic-vs-blocks--summary","content":"Classic vs Blocks — summary"},"1503":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-6","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#related","content":"Related"},"1504":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-7","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","content":"Checkout is where a recalculated cart becomes a\npersisted order. It is also where the classic and\nBlock front-ends diverge the most — the data and order-creation logic is\nshared, but field handling and validation hooks are completely different."},"1505":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-8","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#the-controller","content":"`WC()->checkout()` returns the `WC_Checkout` singleton. It owns the field\ndefinitions, runs validation, and creates the order."},"1506":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-9","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#where-the-field-list-comes-from","content":"The classic checkout fields are assembled from country-aware address fields\nplus account and order fields, then passed through filters:"},"1507":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-10","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#where-the-field-list-comes-from","content":"`woocommerce_checkout_fields` and the address-field filters &#x2A;*do not run\nunder the Checkout Block.** For the Block, call\n`woocommerce_register_additional_checkout_field()` (after `woocommerce_init`)\nwith a `location` of `contact` (saved to the account), `address` (rendered in\nboth billing and shipping), or `order` (saved to the order only), plus\n`id`, `label`, `type` (`text` / `select` / `checkbox`), and optional\n`sanitize_callback` / `validate_callback`."},"1508":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-11","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#order-creation","content":"Under the Block, the equivalent server hook is\n`woocommerce_store_api_checkout_update_order_from_request`, plus the\n`ExtendSchema` update callback for data the Block collected."},"1509":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-12","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#classic-vs-blocks--summary","content":"Concern"},"1510":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-13","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#classic-vs-blocks--summary","content":"Classic"},"1511":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-14","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#classic-vs-blocks--summary","content":"Checkout Block"},"1512":{"id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout-15","page_id":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lifecycle/checkout#classic-vs-bl