()`\n(or `registerExpressPaymentMethod()` for express buttons) from\n`@woocommerce/blocks-registry`."],[924,"**Cookie auth + nonce** — for same-origin requests from a logged-in admin\n(e.g. a custom admin screen), send the `X-WP-Nonce` header from\n`wp_create_nonce( 'wp_rest' )`."],[1266,"**CRUD abstraction** — you are encouraged to read product and order data\nthrough `WC_Product` / `WC_Order` getter methods, not `get_post_meta()`\ndirectly, so that HPOS and lookup tables stay correct. This is covered in\nWooCommerce Data Model."],[1322,"**Dangerous** — editing WooCommerce core files, or depending on private\ninternal behavior that has no stability guarantee. Breaks on update, breaks\nsilently, and breaks other people's expectations."],[43,"**Dangerous** — reverted on the next update"],[40,"**Dangerous** — wrong mechanism entirely, ships broken"],[1394,"**Data model**"],[313,"**Does not belong here** — API reference, step-by-step configuration, code\nrecipes."],[323,"**Does not belong here** — deep internals and extension development (those\nlive in the matching feature section and in Development)."],[328,"**Does not belong here** — exhaustive per-hook catalog entries (those are\nreference pages under the relevant feature section, tagged\n)."],[353,"**Does not belong here** — feature documentation; link back to the subsystem\nbeing debugged."],[368,"**Does not belong here** — feature wishlists framed as bugs."],[343,"**Does not belong here** — general order lifecycle (that is Orders), generic\ndatabase theory."],[363,"**Does not belong here** — general WordPress hardening (link out), server\nconfiguration."],[333,"**Does not belong here** — generic extension mechanics (link to Development\ninstead), unrelated subsystems."],[358,"**Does not belong here** — generic web performance advice unrelated to\nWooCommerce."],[338,"**Does not belong here** — HPOS specifics (its own page below), ORM-style\ntutorials unrelated to WooCommerce."],[348,"**Does not belong here** — subsystem-specific recipes (those live with the\nsubsystem)."],[318,"**Does not belong here** — task guides, admin walkthroughs, per-feature\nreference (those live in the feature sections)."],[1410,"**Emails**"],[1416,"**Extensibility**"],[1431,"**Extension points are first-class.** Most behavior can be changed with an\naction or filter, without touching core or a template."],[1055,"**Good for:** adjusting a price, relabelling a button, adding/removing\ncheckout fields, altering a product query, changing an email recipient,\ntoggling whether a gateway is available."],[1037,"**Good for:** outputting extra markup at a known position, sending a\nnotification, writing a log row, creating related data when an order\ncompletes, enqueueing a script on WooCommerce pages."],[224,"**Gotchas**"],[1387,"**Hooks and filters** — a way to change behavior without editing core."],[220,"**How?**"],[174,"**Incoming webhooks from a payment processor** — verify the processor's\nown signature scheme before trusting the payload; see\nPayments — Webhooks / IPN."],[402,"**Intermediate WordPress developer**"],[107,"**Intermediate WordPress developer** — can build WordPress sites, but\nstruggles with templates, hooks, the cart, checkout, product data, AJAX,\norders, payments, shipping, the database, HPOS, and Blocks."],[222,"**Internally**"],[1429,"**It is open source and readable.** You can follow a request from URL to\ntemplate to hook to data store in actual source code."],[1430,"**It reuses WordPress skills.** Hooks, filters, the plugin model, WP-CLI,\nand the REST API all carry over."],[1433,"**It scales down and up.** The same platform runs a hobby store and a\nhigh-traffic catalog (with real infrastructure work at the top end)."],[1327,"**Locate before you edit.** Identify the layer and lifecycle stage first.\nThe Where Does This Come From?\npattern is built for exactly this."],[1265,"**Lookup tables** — because meta queries are slow, WooCommerce maintains\n`wp_wc_product_meta_lookup` (added in WooCommerce 3.7): one row per product\nwith real columns for `sku`, `min_price` / `max_price`, `stock_status`,\n`stock_quantity`, `onsale`, `rating_count`, `average_rating`, `total_sales`,\n`virtual`, `downloadable`, `tax_status`, `tax_class`. Catalog queries and\nsorting hit this table instead of `wp_postmeta`, and WooCommerce keeps it in\nsync on save."],[1056,"**Must:** always return a value — returning nothing sets it to `null` and\nbreaks everything downstream."],[140,"**No fragment cache to lean on** — every cart/checkout render is a fresh\nAPI call; caching strategy has to be built into the headless front end\nitself rather than inherited from server-rendered fragments."],[1385,"**Options** — site-wide settings."],[1404,"**Order engine**"],[1261,"**Orders are the exception.** With High-Performance Order Storage (HPOS)\nenabled, orders and refunds are stored in dedicated tables, not as\n`shop_order&#x60; posts. Treating an order as \"just a post\" is the single most\ncommon outdated assumption in older WooCommerce tutorials. See the HPOS\nsection &#x2A;(planned)* and\nWooCommerce Data Model."],[1406,"**Payments & shipping**"],[1438,"**Performance requires deliberate work** at scale — object caching, a\ntuned host, careful extension choices, and sometimes a headless front-end."],[1436,"**Plugin sprawl is a real risk.** Every extension is code running in your\nrequest path; conflicts and performance regressions come with the model."],[1321,"**Possible but risky** — overriding a template by copying it into your\ntheme, or replacing a whole subsystem. Sometimes the right call, but you now\nown that copy forever and must re-check it on every WooCommerce update."],[1383,"**Posts and pages** — arbitrary content, stored in `wp_posts`."],[1329,"**Prefer the highest-safety layer that can do the job.** Hook or filter\nfirst; template override only when a hook cannot reach it; never core."],[1784,"**Prices entered with or without tax** (`woocommerce_prices_include_tax`) is\na store-wide decision that changes how every price is interpreted. Combined\nwith \"display prices in shop/cart including or excluding tax\", it is the\nsource of most \"the total is off by a cent\" reports. Changing it on a live\nstore re-interprets every existing price."],[311,"**Priority** —"],[321,"**Priority** —"],[341,"**Priority** —"],[346,"**Priority** —"],[351,"**Priority** —"],[356,"**Priority** —"],[361,"**Priority** —"],[366,"**Priority** —"],[336,"**Priority** —  concepts,\n schema reference."],[331,"**Priority** —  for the concepts,\n for the reference tables within them."],[316,"**Priority** —  to"],[326,"**Priority** —  to"],[763,"**Priority** and **accepted args** work exactly as for actions — argument 3\nand 4 of `add_filter()`. Ask for every context parameter you need; they are\nonly passed up to the count you declare."],[1264,"**Product data** — almost every product field is post meta under an\nunderscore-prefixed key: `_regular_price`, `_sale_price`, `_price`, `_sku`,\n`_stock`, `_stock_status`, `_weight`, `_length` / `_width` / `_height`,\n`_tax_class`, `_manage_stock`, `_downloadable`, `_virtual`, and more."],[236,"**Purpose** — accomplish one concrete task."],[364,"**Purpose** — an honest catalog of what WooCommerce does not do well, and\nwhen to choose another approach."],[344,"**Purpose** — cross-cutting \"how to change X safely\" patterns that span\nmultiple subsystems."],[242,"**Purpose** — diagnose a class of unexpected behavior."],[257,"**Purpose** — document a REST or Store API resource."],[254,"**Purpose** — document a table or a storage pattern."],[248,"**Purpose** — document one action or filter."],[251,"**Purpose** — document one classic template file."],[233,"**Purpose** — explain an idea or mechanism (e.g. \"the cart session\",\n\"template overrides\")."],[260,"**Purpose** — help choose between approaches (extension vs custom, classic\nvs Blocks, WooCommerce vs another stack)."],[339,"**Purpose** — how order storage works with HPOS: the tables, the\ncompatibility mode, the migration, and what changes for developers."],[349,"**Purpose** — how to diagnose unexpected WooCommerce behavior methodically."],[334,"**Purpose** — how WooCommerce stores data: core WordPress tables it uses,\nWooCommerce's custom tables, meta usage, query patterns, and a full\ncolumn-by-column schema lookup."],[239,"**Purpose** — look up exact details (a hook signature, a template path list,\na settings key)."],[329,"**Purpose** — one deep, self-contained treatment per subsystem: what it is,\nwhere it lives, its lifecycle, its data, its hooks/filters/templates/blocks,\nits gotchas, and its safe customization patterns. (Customers is currently\nfolded into Checkout and Orders; it may get its own page later.)"],[309,"**Purpose** — orient a WordPress developer: what WooCommerce is, why it\nexists, how it differs from plain WordPress work, and how to think about it."],[245,"**Purpose** — show how a subsystem is built and how data moves through it."],[319,"**Purpose** — the admin-facing configuration surface: settings, and the\nsetup of products, customers, orders, payments, shipping, and taxes."],[324,"**Purpose** — the extension toolkit: hooks, filters, templates, shortcodes,\nblocks, AJAX, REST, and JavaScript — how each mechanism works and when to\nreach for it."],[314,"**Purpose** — the load-bearing concepts: the WordPress features WooCommerce\nbuilds on, WooCommerce's own architecture, its data model, and its\nextension model."],[359,"**Purpose** — the WooCommerce-specific security surface."],[354,"**Purpose** — where WooCommerce spends time and how to reduce it."],[792,"**Query Monitor** (plugin) lists every hook fired on the current request,\nwith callbacks and file references."],[1320,"**Recommended extension** — official hooks, filters, and APIs; supported\ntemplate mechanisms; a properly structured plugin or `mu-plugin`. Survives\nupdates. This is the default answer."],[22,"**Recommended**"],[25,"**Recommended**"],[28,"**Recommended**"],[31,"**Recommended**"],[34,"**Recommended** (for Blocks)"],[228,"**Related**"],[1331,"**Respect classic vs Blocks.** The same customization can require different\ntechniques depending on which cart/checkout implementation is active."],[1412,"**REST & Store API**"],[173,"**REST API** — a consumer key/secret pair is scoped to Read, Write, or\nRead/Write, but ultimately executes with the capabilities of the WordPress\nuser it was generated for. A key generated against an over-privileged user\nis a bigger blast radius than the key's own read/write label suggests —\ngenerate integration keys against a dedicated, minimally-privileged user."],[37,"**Risky** — you now own a forked file"],[226,"**Safer alternative**"],[1701,"**Server** — a class extending\n`Automattic\\WooCommerce\\Blocks\\Payments\\Integrations\\AbstractPaymentMethodType`,\nregistered on the `woocommerce_blocks_payment_method_type_registration`\naction (inside a `woocommerce_blocks_loaded` callback) via\n`$payment_method_registry->register( new My_Method() )`."],[84,"**Settings → Advanced → REST API**; see REST API"],[241,"**Skeleton** — `PageMeta` (usually ) → one-line\nsummary → reference table(s) → `VersionNote` → minimal example → Related."],[259,"**Skeleton** — `PageMeta` → endpoint(s) → auth → request/response shape →\nexample → rate/permission notes → Related."],[238,"**Skeleton** — `PageMeta` → Goal → Prerequisites → `Steps` → Result →\n`SafetyLevel` (where the code belongs) → Gotchas → Related."],[247,"**Skeleton** — `PageMeta` → One-paragraph overview → `LayerStack` or\n`Lifecycle` diagram → component-by-component walkthrough → extension surface\n→ Related."],[253,"**Skeleton** — `PageMeta` → path → what renders it → variables in scope →\nhooks fired inside → override procedure (`SafetyLevel` risky) → Blocks\nequivalent → Related."],[250,"**Skeleton** — `PageMeta` → signature (name, type, parameters, default\npriority) → What fires it / where → When to use → When