ment back to the layer that produced it.\" />"],[120,"<Card title=\"Where Does This Come From?\" href=\"/docs/introduction/where-does-this-come-from\" description=\"WooDoc's signature pattern for tracing any WooCommerce element to its source.\" />"],[1336,"<Card title=\"Why WooCommerce?\" href=\"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce\" description=\"The trade-offs you are working within.\" />"],[118,"<Card title=\"Why WooCommerce?\" href=\"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce\" description=\"What it solves, what it adds to WordPress, the trade-offs, and when it is the wrong tool.\" />"],[1297,"<Card title=\"Why WooCommerce?\" href=\"/docs/introduction/why-woocommerce\" description=\"What WooCommerce adds to the WordPress base described here.\" />"],[1295,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Architecture\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture\" description=\"How WooCommerce boots on top of this lifecycle and organizes itself in memory.\" />"],[1219,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Architecture\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture\" description=\"The CRUD / data-store layer that abstracts all of this storage.\" />"],[1087,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Architecture\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-architecture\" description=\"The shared core that all four mechanisms hook into.\" />"],[576,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Data Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model\" description=\"Orders and order items in the overall entity model.\" />"],[1168,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Data Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model\" description=\"The entities the CRUD layer manages and where each is stored.\" />"],[551,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Data Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model\" description=\"The entities these tables back, and their CRUD classes.\" />"],[679,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Data Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model\" description=\"The entities these tables back.\" />"],[773,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Data Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model\" description=\"The WC_Data objects whose getters these filters wrap.\" />"],[1296,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Data Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model\" description=\"What WooCommerce stores, in which tables, and how to read it correctly.\" />"],[1768,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Data Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/woocommerce-data-model\" description=\"Where product and variation data is stored.\" />"],[1169,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Extension Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/extension-model\" description=\"Hooks, filters, templates, and blocks as one composable system.\" />"],[46,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Extension Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/extension-model\" description=\"The four mechanisms this page assumes — read that one first.\" />"],[1022,"<Card title=\"WooCommerce Extension Model\" href=\"/docs/foundations/extension-model\" description=\"Where template overrides sit among the four mechanisms.\" />"],[1220,"<Card title=\"WordPress Fundamentals\" href=\"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals\" description=\"Post types, meta, and options — the primitives this model is built from.\" />"],[1167,"<Card title=\"WordPress Fundamentals\" href=\"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals\" description=\"The request lifecycle and hook system this bootstrap plugs into.\" />"],[934,"<Card title=\"WordPress Fundamentals\" href=\"/docs/foundations/wordpress-fundamentals\" description=\"The WordPress REST layer both APIs are built on.\" />"],[1313,"> \"How do I change the displayed price?\""],[1324,"> **\"Just because I can change it there does not mean I should.\"**"],[231,"> **Concept → Location → Decision → Implementation → Warning → Example → Related**"],[433,"> **Concept → Location → Decision → Implementation → Warning → Example → Related**"],[384,"> Give developers enough understanding and visibility into WooCommerce that it\n> stops feeling like a black box."],[1333,"> WooCommerce work is multi-dimensional. A change has a **layer**, a\n> **lifecycle stage**, a **safety level**, and a **ripple**. Name all four\n> before you write code."],[1210,"$product = wc\\_get\\_product( $id ); then\n$product->get\\_price(), ->get\\_stock\\_quantity(),\n->is\\_in\\_stock(). The getters read from the right place\n(lookup table, meta, or computed) — raw meta reads do not."],[1342,"1\\. What am I looking at?"],[1216,"11.0 added **guest order claiming**: a logged-in customer can link past\nguest-checkout orders (matched by email, with email verification) to their\naccount, after which those orders show in their order history."],[1162,"11.0.1 moved guest session cookies to a stronger, salted hashing scheme\n(with backward compatibility for existing cookies). The table name and the\n`woocommerce_cleanup_sessions` schedule are unchanged."],[1343,"2\\. Where does it come from?"],[1344,"3\\. What controls it?"],[1345,"4\\. What can I safely modify?"],[1346,"5\\. What should I avoid?"],[65,"A \"Troubleshooting\" / \"Health Check\" style plugin that lets *you* see the\nsite with plugins disabled while other visitors still see the live site is\nthe safe way to run this bisection in production."],[760,"A **filter** is a value passing through a named checkpoint:\n`$value = apply_filters( 'filter_name', $value, ...$context )`. Your callback\nreceives the value, returns a possibly-changed version, and WooCommerce uses\nwhat you return. Filters are how you change *what something is* — a price, a\nlabel, a list of fields, a query — without editing core."],[10,"A **must-use plugin** (a file dropped in `wp-content/mu-plugins/`).\nWordPress loads every file there automatically, before regular plugins'\n`plugins_loaded`, and it never appears in the deactivatable **Plugins**\nlist. Trade-off: no activation/deactivation hooks, no auto-updates, and\n(native WordPress limitation) only files directly in `mu-plugins/` load —\na plugin that ships in its own subdirectory needs a one-line loader file\nat the top level that `require`s it."],[227,"A better extension point, if one exists."],[4,"A Blocks customization, worked end to end"],[1300,"A blog site is one dimension. A store is several."],[1325,"A brochure site has pages. WooCommerce has a **lifecycle** that pages are\nwindows into:"],[80,"A caching layer (object cache or page cache) serving a stale page before the lookup table sync completed"],[1243,"A catalog product"],[964,"A configurable product grid — the modern, unified one (attributes: `ids`, `category`, `tag`, `limit`, `columns`, `orderby`, `on_sale`, `best_selling`, `top_rated`, …)"],[1249,"A coupon"],[1217,"A coupon is a `shop_coupon` post whose meta holds the rule. The\n`discount_type` is one of `percent`, `fixed_cart`, or `fixed_product`; other\nmeta keys include `coupon_amount`, `individual_use`, `usage_limit`,\n`usage_limit_per_user`, `limit_usage_to_x_items`, `date_expires`,\n`free_shipping`, `product_ids` / `exclude_product_ids`, `product_categories` /\n`exclude_product_categories`, `minimum_amount`, `maximum_amount`. `WC_Coupon`\nreads it; the cart totals pipeline applies it."],[880,"A coupon was applied / removed on the checkout form"],[155,"A custom My Account endpoint, REST route, or AJAX handler that reads an\norder or customer by an ID taken from the request **without** confirming\nit belongs to the current user is an IDOR: any logged-in customer can\nsubstitute another order ID and read (or, worse, modify) someone else's\ndata. Check `$order->get_customer_id() === get_current_user_id()` (or the\nequivalent capability for staff) before returning anything."],[421,"A developer arriving on any WooDoc page should be able to answer quickly:"],[303,"A developer cannot properly understand WooCommerce without this."],[103,"A developer-first WooCommerce **engineering reference** — not a \"how to run\nyour store\" tutorial and not a marketing site."],[546,"A direct, read-only query against the appropriate **lookup table**\n(`wc_product_meta_lookup`, the `wc_order_*_lookup` analytics tables) is\nthe sanctioned fast path — it is what WooCommerce's own reports use."],[1727,"A display container that links to other simple products; not itself purchasable"],[762,"A filter callback that does not return sets the value to\nnull. This is the most common filter bug: an early\nreturn;, a missing return on one branch, or a\nvar\\_dump() left in. The button vanishes, the price becomes\nempty, the field list is wiped."],[1054,"A filter is `apply_filters( 'some_filter', $value, $context… )`. Your callback\nreceives `$value`, returns a (possibly modified) version, and WooCommerce uses\nwhat you return."],[136,"A filter or action that runs **once per product in a loop** — a catalog\npage, a cart with many line items, an export — turns any per-call cost\n(an uncached query, an external API call, expensive string formatting) into\nan N+1 problem invisible in isolation but severe at scale."],[966,"A full single-product layout for one product"],[1681,"A gateway extends `WC_Payment_Gateway` and is registered via the\n`woocommerce_payment_gateways` filter."],[1481,"A hash of the product data, so a price change invalidates a stale session line"],[138,"A headless build talks to WooCommerce entirely through the\nStore API — the classic\n`wc-ajax`/cart-fragments machinery does not apply, since there is no\nserver-rendered page for it to refresh. The relevant costs shift to:"],[85,"A hook callback \"never fires\""],[74,"A JS error stopped `checkout.js`, or a `woocommerce_checkout_process`/`_before_order_pay` callback exited without a WooCommerce-aware error"],[1479,"A live `WC_Product` object for this line — this is what pricing reads"],[726,"A minimal Slot/Fill"],[221,"A minimal, correct, copyable implementation."],[1489,"A negative fee is how you apply a programmatic discount that a coupon cannot\nexpress."],[1724,"A parent with attributes; buyable variations are its children"],[1680,"A payment gateway is an adapter between WooCommerce's order and an external\npayment processor. WooCommerce defines the interface; the gateway implements\n`process_payment()` and, usually, a webhook handler. This page is the shape of\nthat interface, not a guide to any one processor."],[1399,"A per-visitor cart, session persistence for guests and logged-in users, and AJAX cart fragments."],[988,"A plugin can provide templates too"],[1733,"A product carries three stored price fields and one computed one:"],[1714,"A product is the catalog entity everything else in WooCommerce is priced and\nstocked against. This page covers what a product *is* at runtime, how the\nprice you see is assembled, and how stock is tracked. The storage layout is in\nWooCommerce Data Model;\nthis page is about behavior."],[1208,"A product is the most WordPress-shaped entity: a `product` post plus a lot of\nmeta plus taxonomy terms."],[1446,"A purpose-built system on a relational schema you control may be a better\nfit than a CMS-shaped model — evaluate carefully rather than assume."],[1164,"A recurring architectural fact: the **data and business logic layer is\nshared**, but the storefront presentation exists in two implementations."],[1255,"A refund against an order"],[1664,"A refund covering the full total moves the order to `refunded`."],[1633,"A refund covering the whole total"],[1662,"A refund is a **negative child order** (`WC_Order_Refund`, post type\n`shop_order_refund` in legacy mode):"],[9,"A regular plugin. It shows up in **Plugins**, can be versioned and\nupdated independently of the theme, survives a theme change, and can use\nactivation/deactivation hooks to set up or clean up its own data."],[1258,"A REST API webhook subscription"],[930,"A route with 'permission\\_callback' => '\\_\\_return\\_true' is\npublic. If it reads or writes store data, that is a data-exposure bug.\nAlways supply a real permission callback."],[941,"A shortcode is a `[bracketed]` token in post content that WordPress replaces\nwith rendered output. WooCommerce registers a set of them through the\n`WC_Shortcodes` class on `init`. Two groups matter for different reasons."],[1311,"A store forces you to think in **multiple dimensions at once**, because a\nsingle visible thing is the result of business rules, a lifecycle, data, and\noften an external service:"],[1693,"A stored reference to a payment method (`gateway_id`, `token`, `user_id`, `type`, `is_default`; CC adds `last4`, `expiry_month/year`, `card_type`) — never raw card data"],[1077,"A template override is a **maintained fork of one file**. Each core template\ncarries an @version docblock; WooCommerce → Status → System\nStatus lists every overridden template whose @version is behind\nthe current core template (\"version X is out of date. The core version is\nY\"). When WooCommerce changes that template, your copy does not get the\nchange and can silently drop new markup, hooks, or accessibility fixes. Use\nonly when no hook or filter reaches what you need."],[1411,"A templated transactional email system with per-email settings."],[1312,"A theme developer asks:"],[1688,"A webhook endpoint with no signature verification lets anyone mark any order\npaid. Verify the processor's signature on every call, and treat the payload\nas untrusted input."],[1314,"A WooCommerce developer eventually learns to ask:"],[1382,"A WordPress install gives you:"],[1214,"A WordPress user with role `customer` (capabilities: `read` plus\nWooCommerce's own `read_private_shop_orders` etc. for their own data),\nplus user meta for billing/shipping address, plus a row in\n`wp_wc_customer_lookup` for Analytics. Order history is every order with\ntheir `customer_id`."],[1120,"Accessor"],[420,"Accuracy is a hard rule: no invented hooks, paths, or behavior."],[380,"Accuracy rules"],[1040,"Action"],[24,"Action pair — `woocommerce_product_options_general_product_data` (render) + `woocommerce_process_product_meta` (save)"],[1154,"Action Scheduler proxy"],[1073,"Action. Hook the position, echo or do your thing."],[1026,"Actions — change *what happens*"],[1028,"Actions vs filters — the test"],[1743,"Active price"],[23,"Add a custom field to the product admin screen"],[32,"Add a field to the Checkout **Block**"],[29,"Add a field to the classic checkout"],[1757,"Add a field to the product editor"],[1759,"Add a product type"],[1592,"Add CC/BCC or custom headers"],[468,"Add diagrams that do not answer a specific developer question."],[1590,"Add rows after the order table"],[857,"Add-to-cart succeeded (params include the fragments and cart hash)"],[14,"Adding a \"gift note\" field to checkout shows how the mechanisms in the\nBlocks layer\ncombine in practice — and how differently the same feature is built classic\nvs. Blocks:"],[897,"Adding a custom route"],[1775,"Adding a shipping method"],[684,"Adding your own front-end AJAX"],[1403,"Address fields, validation, payment method selection, order creation, and the \"thank you\" / order-received flow."],[1545,"Admin"],[1548,"Admin"],[1551,"Admin"],[1627,"Admin marks it, or auto for downloads-only"],[496,"Advanced engineering topics driven by real developer questions."],[1115,"After `WooCommerce::init()` has run"],[680,"AJAX"],[827,"AJAX add-to-cart from product loops"],[849,"All are registered in `WC_Frontend_Scripts` and enqueued only on the pages\nthat need them (cart script on the cart page, and so on)."],[599,"All tables below are prefixed with the WordPress table prefix (`wp_` by\ndefault) and defined in `WC_Install::get_schema()`, except the HPOS order\ntables, defined by the orders data store. This is a lookup page — read\nDatabase first for how these tables relate,\nand HPOS for the order tables specifically."],[1207,"All the product and order classes ultimately extend `WC_Data`, the base class\nthat provides the getter/setter/`save()` contract and delegates persistence to\na data store."],[8,"All three can hold the exact same `add_action()` / `add_filter()` call. The\nchoice is about **lifecycle and ownership**, not capability."],[1262,"Alongside each post, WordPress keeps arbitrary key/value pairs in\n`wp_postmeta` (`post_id`, `meta_key`, `meta_value`), read with\n`get_post_meta()`. It is schemaless and flexible, and expensive to query at\nscale because `meta_value` is a long text column with no useful index."],[274,"Always label the context: **theme**, **plugin**, **mu-plugin**,\n**functions.php**, **JavaScript**, **CSS**, or **template override**."],[545,"Always the CRUD layer — `wc_get_product()`, `wc_get_order()`,\n`new WC_Customer()`. It is correct under both legacy and HPOS storage, and\nkeeps the lookup tables in sync on write."],[1730,"An \"affiliate\" product — the add-to-cart button links off-site"],[781,"An **action** is a named moment in execution where WooCommerce (or WordPress)\ncalls `do_action( 'hook_name', ...$args )`. Any code registered against that\nname runs at that point. Actions are how you make something *happen* —\noutput markup, send a message, write a record — without editing core."],[62,"An **out-of-date template** (\"version X is out of date. The core version\nis Y\") on this page is a leading cause of \"this update broke my site\" —\nsee Templates.\nCheck this list before assuming the bug is in WooCommerce itself."],[1036,"An action is a point in execution where WooCommerce calls\n`do_action( 'some_hook', $context… )`. Your callback runs there for effect;\nits return value is discarded."],[855,"An AJAX add-to-cart request is about to be sent"],[714,"An AJAX handler with no nonce check and no capability check is a CSRF hole —\nworse if it writes data or reveals another customer's order. Every custom\nhandler: nonce first, capability second, then the work."],[1487,"An applied coupon is stored in the session as a code. During calculation\n`WC_Discounts` loads each `WC_Coupon`, validates it against the current cart\n(usage limits, product/category restrictions, min/max spend, expiry), and\napplies the discount by `discount_type`\n(`percent` / `fixed_cart` / `fixed_product`)."],[859,"An item was removed via AJAX"],[1252,"An order"],[562,"An order as a `shop_order` post meant every field — status, totals,\naddresses, payment details — was a separate row in `wp_postmeta`, an\nunindexed-by-value table shared with every other post type on the site.\nHigh-volume stores felt this as slow order queries, lock contention during\ncheckout, and a `wp_postmeta` table that dwarfed everything else in the\ndatabase."],[167,"An order carries name, address, email, phone, and IP — all PII — whether or\nnot the store is otherwise GDPR-scoped. WooCommerce ships privacy tooling\nthat plugs into WordPress core's own personal-data tools rather than\nreinventing them:"],[1211,"An order is a container; the money and the goods live in its **items**. Even\nunder classic storage, order items were never post meta — they have always\nbeen in dedicated tables."],[1610,"An order is the durable record of a purchase. Its **status** drives almost\nevery side effect in WooCommerce — emails, stock, downloads, reports — so the\nstatus-transition hooks are the most important surface on this subsystem."],[1401,"An ordered calculation of line totals, discounts, fees, tax, and shipping."],[593,"Analytics lookup tables"],[209,"Answers"],[170,"Any custom code that receives or logs a raw PAN, CVV, or full card number —\neven transiently, even to a debug log — pulls your server into full PCI-DSS\nscope. Log gateway responses, not raw request payloads; a `WC_Logger` entry\nis not a secure place for payment details."],[1053,"Any order status transition"],[1116,"Anything depending on the `product` post type or WooCommerce taxonomies"],[1282,"API"],[1289,"API keys (consumer key/secret) or cookie auth + nonce"],[925,"API keys are full credentials for whatever scope they carry. A Read-Write\nkey can create orders and read every customer's PII. Scope them minimally,\nstore them as secrets, and revoke unused ones."],[191,"API page"